\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar gives back gains after rise to two-week highs, yen firms\b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2016\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Yen moves higher after sinking on officials' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk\par \par \uc2 * Aussie resumes slide after crude oil's about-face\par \par \uc2 * Kiwi soars after RBNZ opts to refrain from steps to cool housing\par \par \uc2 By Lisa Twaronite and Ian Chua\par \par \uc2 TOKYO/SYDNEY, May 11 (Reuters) - The dollar dipped on Wednesday as investors locked in gains following its steep rise against the yen after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings from Japanese officials.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which tracks the greenback against a basket of six rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , shed 0.2 percent to 94.126, moving away from its two-week high of 94.356 set overnight.\par \par \uc2 However, it remained well above a 15-month trough of 91.919 set on May 3.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.4 percent to 108.83 after climbing to a two-week high of 109.38 yen early in the Asian session. It moved back toward last week's low of 105.55, which marked its lowest since October 2014.\par \par \uc2 The euro slipped about 0.3 percent to 123.90 yen after notching a two-week high of 124.415 overnight after bouncing off a three-year bottom of 121.48 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had suffered losses in late April when the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  held off from expanding monetary stimulus, touching off a rally in the yen that stoked investors' fears that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, many expect that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be wary of conducting direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before it hosts a G7 meeting later this month, as Tokyo is sensitive to criticism that it is trying to engineer a weaker yen.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so easily," said Ayako Sera, market strategist at Sumitomo Trust and Banking. "But the recent comments from officials provided investors with good timing to unwind some of their long positions."\par \par \uc2 Koichi Hamada, a key economic adviser to Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 , was the latest to sound a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market warning.\par \par \uc2 Hamada said on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the yen strengthens to 90-95 per dollar, even if that upsets the United States.\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday's comments from Japanese officials hinting at possible \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the JPY, combined with the lift in European and U.S. equity markets have undermined JPY," noted Elias Haddad, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commonwealth Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, recent dovish comments from core \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  members and weaker-than-expected job gains in April continue to cap the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The euro added 0.1 percent to $1.13810, though it remained below a 2016 high of $1.16160 hit on May 3.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar slipped about 0.1 percent to $0.7357 moving back toward a two-month low of 73 cents touched on Tuesday, as oil prices gave up their overnight gains.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar stole some limelight, rising 0.6 percent to 68 U.S. cents, climbing well away from a recent low of $0.6717.\par \par \uc2 Markets had sold the kiwi on Tuesday on speculation the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  (RBNZ) would introduce new measures to curb Auckland's housing market. When the RBNZ held off from that course on Wednesday investors were quick to unwind those moves. (Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-11T04:48:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160511ec5b000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
