\par\par \b \uc2 Asian Morning Briefing: Stocks Climb as Oil Prices Bounce Back\b0\par\par\uc2 2,229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2016\par 23:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS AT A GLANCE\par \par \uc2 (Data as of approximately 5 p.m. ET) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      LAST      CHANGE  % CHG \par DJIA                 17928.35  222.44  1.26% \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2                4809.88   59.67   1.26% \par S&P 500              2084.39   25.7    1.25% \par Japan: Nikkei 225    16565.19  349.16  2.15% \par Hang Seng            20242.68  85.87   0.43% \par Shanghai Composite   2832.59   0.48    0.02% \par S&P \f28 \uc2 \f2 BSE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sensex       25772.53  83.67   0.33% \par Australia: S&P/ASX   5342.8    22.1    0.42% \par UK: FTSE 100         6156.65   41.84   0.68% \par  \par  \par                     PRICE CHG  YIELD \par U.S. 2 Year          -1/32     0.722 \par U.S. 5 Year          -1/32     1.2 \par U.S. 10 Year         -2/32     1.752 \par Australia 10 Year    5/32      2.315 \par China 10 Year        2/32      2.909 \par India 10 Year       0/32       7.427 \par Japan 10 Year        -3/32     -0.097 \par German 10 Year       -1/32     0.131 \par  \par  \par                           LAST(MID)  CHANGE \par Australia $ (AUD/USD)     0.7365     0.0049 \par Yen (USD/JPY)             109.29     0.95 \par S. Korean Won (USD/KRW)   1171.18    -4.39 \par Chinese Yuan (USD/CNY)    6.5178     0.0009 \par Euro (EUR/USD)            1.1372     -0.0013 \par WSJ Dollar Index          86.63      0.05 \par  \par  \par               LAST    CHANGE  % CHG \par Crude Oil     44.67   1.23    2.83% \par Brent Crude   45.6    1.97    4.52% \par Gold          1268.1  1.5     0.12% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SNAPSHOT:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A broad rally bolstered by rebounding oil prices Tuesday drove major U.S. indexes to their biggest gains in weeks. Gold prices settled lower in U.S. trading as investors sought out riskier assets. The dollar rose against the yen after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned that it was ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to strengthen. \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds were little changed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPENING CALL:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese market has some demand potential to mop up global natural-gas volumes, but panelists at the Flame gas conference in Amsterdam displayed some skepticism about the extent of this. "We have to recognize that there are a lot of uncertainties with the China gas market," says Xianfang Ren, China market fundamentals manager at BG Group. Economic growth in slowing in China, which is also cooling expansion in the gas market. This will likely continue for the next decade, she says. And this demand will have to come at the expense of coal, equivalent to up to 400 million tons worth, she adds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A broad rally bolstered by rebounding oil prices drove major U.S. indexes to their biggest gains in weeks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock moves have been relatively small in the U.S. recently, after markets fell sharply and recovered earlier this year. Major indexes last notched a daily gain of at least 1% in mid-April.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All 10 sectors of the S&P 500 rose Tuesday, with gains in energy and financial stocks outpacing the broader market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 222 points, or 1.3%, to 17928. The Nasdaq Composite and S&P 500 each rose 1.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Assets investors consider havens such as gold and \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt were steady, a sign many weren't convinced that the rally will last, traders and analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You have a very thin market without a lot of conviction," said Rob Bernstone, managing director of equity trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading volume was relatively light compared with other days when stocks have gained sharply, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are struggling to reconcile a recent rebound in stock prices with a lackluster earnings season and concerns about the health of the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I see OK earnings and OK valuations, but nothing in a world of uncertainty that's making investors want to pay up for stocks," said David Lafferty, chief market strategist at Natixis Global Asset Management.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.5%, adding about 27 points to the Dow industrials. \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 1.4%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in Asia reversed earlier losses to end mostly higher on Tuesday, led by a surge in Japanese stocks after officials warned that the government could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against a sharp rise in the yen.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar rose against the yen Tuesday, after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned that it was ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to strengthen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was recently up 0.9% at Yen109.27. The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the buck against a basket of 16 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was up 0.1% at 86.62.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taro Aso\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday he was "prepared to undertake \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the yen rose further, the latest official to warn that the country won't tolerate an excessively strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the same time, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials have their stepped up hawkish rhetoric in recent days, helping the dollar move higher. On Friday, St. Louis Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Bullard\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned that the very slow pace of U.S. rate increases seen by financial markets is likely at odds with what the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could deliver. Higher rates are a boon to the dollar, as they make the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more attractive to yield-seeking investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent comments show "there could be a higher risk of a rate (increase) in the months ahead than the recent tone of U.S. economic data alone may be suggesting," said Omer Esiner, chief market analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of commodity producers, as oil prices rose. The greenback was recently down 1.2% against the Brazilian real at 3.4750. It gave up 1.1% against the Mexican peso, to 17.98.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BONDS:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds were little changed Tuesday as solid demand on a three-year note auction offset higher stock and oil prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The resilience of the haven bond market suggests many investors remain cautious in chasing riskier markets amid a muddy global economic growth and inflation outlook. The $24 billion sale of three-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes generated the strongest demand since January.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  note was 1.760%, compared with 1.759% Monday. Bond yields and prices move inversely to each other.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both the S&P 500 stock index and U.S. crude oil futures rose by more than 1% Tuesday afternoon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields remain stubbornly low despite a sharp rebound in stock and oil prices since mid-February. That has confounded many bond traders and made investors hesitant to place large negative wagers on bond prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the other hand, some money managers say higher bond yields present a buying opportunity as they don't expect a large increase in bond yields without robust economic growth or a pick-up in inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The new three-year notes were offered at a slim yield of 0.875%. It attracted 61.5% indirect bidding, a gauge of demand from foreign investors. That was the latest sign of solid buying interest from foreign investors who are grappling with a large number of government debt in Japan and the eurozone yielding below zero.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In that light, U.S. bonds remain an attractive bargain despite low yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The auction results also suggest that many investors expect the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be very slow in raising interest rates, a factor that would reduce the risk of a large increase in yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is a broad sense of doubt that the Fed is going to [raise rates] again in 2016," said Thomas Simons, vice president and money-market economist in the Fixed Income Group at Jefferies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices rose on expectations that supply outages from Canada to Nigeria would help to alleviate the global glut of crude.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Light, sweet crude for June delivery settled up $1.22, or 2.8%, to $44.66 a barrel on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Brent, the global benchmark, rose $1.89, or 4.3%, to $45.52 a barrel on \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil-production outages in some regions are helping reduce crude output, boosting expectations that the global glut of crude that has battered prices since mid-2014 could be shrinking. But analysts say that these disruptions are temporary and most of those barrels will come back online soon. In addition, Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil company said Tuesday that it plans to increase its output this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts and traders also expect U.S. inventory data set for release Wednesday to show that domestic crude inventories rose to a new record last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wildfires in Canada's oil-rich Alberta province have removed about 1.6 million barrels a day of production, or more than 1% of global supply, from the market, according to consulting firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Energy Aspects\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The extent and duration of the outages remains uncertain. Canada is a major exporter of oil to the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market is trying to assess the damage," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Phil Flynn\f28 \uc2 \f2 , analyst at Price Futures Group in Chicago. "It's definitely a supportive factor."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices settled lower in U.S. trading, as investors sought out riskier assets amid a stock-market rally and an increase in oil prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TODAY'S HEADLINES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Disney Results Boosted by Recent Films\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Disney\f28 \uc2 \f2 's earnings rose a weaker-than-expected 1.7% in the latest quarter. as the popularity of the films "Star Wars" and "Zootopia" were offset by costs related to its new park in Shanghai.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2  Rebuts Claim It Suppresses Conservative News\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2  denied allegations from former workers who said the social media site suppressed news about conservative issues on its popular "trending" news feature.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electronic Arts\f28 \uc2 \f2  Leans on 'Star Wars' and Sports to Power Profit\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electronic Arts\f28 \uc2 \f2  closed out its fiscal year with better-than-expected revenue and profit, aided by its "Star Wars" and sports franchises.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman, Jefferies Put \f28 \uc2 \f2 LendingClub\f28 \uc2 \f2  Deals on Hold\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The banks are reviewing events that led to the ousting of LendingClub Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Renaud Laplanche\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which could delay or jeopardize a number of closely watched securitization deals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wall Street Firms Under Investigation for Treatment of Retail Investors\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10 May 2016 17:31 ET \par Asian Morning Briefing: Stocks Climb as Oil -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal and state authorities are investigating whether Wall Street firms that handle millions of orders annually for retail clients have lived up to their obligation to provide the best possible treatment for those investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wal-Mart\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sues \f28 \uc2 \f2 Visa\f28 \uc2 \f2  Over Chip-Enabled Debit Card Transactions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wal-Mart\f28 \uc2 \f2  filed a lawsuit against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Visa\f28 \uc2 \f2 , saying the payments network is preventing the retailing giant from requiring customers to verify their purchases with a personal identification number when they use a chip-enabled debit card.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed's Williams: Highly Unlikely U.S. Would Go Negative on Rates\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 San Francisco Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Williams\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it is highly unlikely the U.S. would need to push interest rates into negative territory to spur economic growth, in an online session with question-and-answer website \f28 \uc2 \f2 Quora\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dell Plans $16 Billion Investment-Grade Bond Sale\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dell\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to begin marketing around $16 billion of secured bonds this week as part of its acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 EMC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the matter said, as the computer maker tries to take advantage of a hot market for highly rated debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amazon Launches YouTube-Like Video Service\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com\f28 \uc2 \f2  is intensifying its rivalry with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  with a new ad-supported video service that resembles \f28 \uc2 \f2 YouTube\f28 \uc2 \f2 , letting anyone upload clips.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Bangladesh, Swift Join in Effort to Trace Stolen Funds\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangladesh's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and internal financial messaging provider Swift will work together to trace the $81 million still missing from Bangladesh's account at the Fed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RECENT DJ EXCLUSIVES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wal-Mart\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sues \f28 \uc2 \f2 Visa\f28 \uc2 \f2  Over Chip-Enabled Debit Card Transactions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gap: Being Big Is Out of Fashion -- Heard on the Street\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Stock Is Cheap for a Reason -- Ahead of the Tape\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil Bust Gives Billionaire Deal-Maker Buyer's Remorse\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman, Jefferies Pause Buying \f28 \uc2 \f2 LendingClub\f28 \uc2 \f2  Loans\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TODAY'S CALENDAR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Times in GMT, followed by country and event)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2100 NZ RBNZ Financial Stability Report\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2245 NZ Mar Accommodation Survey\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2300 SKA Apr Economically Active Population Survey, incl Unemployment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350 JPN Apr International Reserves / Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 0030 AUS May \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  - Melbourne Institute Consumer Sentiment Survey\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0100 PHI Mar Merchandise Export Performance\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0130 AUS Mar Housing Finance\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0400 AUS May Monthly Leading Indicator of Employment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0500 JPN Mar Indexes of Business Conditions - Preliminary Release\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0600 GER Mar Manufacturing turnover\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0700 THA Bank of Thailand Monetary Policy Committee meeting and decision\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0830 UK Mar UK monthly industrial production figures\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0900 GER Q2 Ifo World Economic Climate\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1000 FRA Mar OECD Composite Leading Indicators\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1100 US 05/06 MBA Weekly Mortgage Applications Survey\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1315 UK \f28 \uc2 \f2 George Osborne\f28 \uc2 \f2  questioned by MPs on \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  membership\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1400 UK Apr NIESR Monthly GDP Estimates\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1430 US 05/06 EIA Weekly Petroleum Status Report\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1800 US Apr Monthly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Statement of Receipts & Outlays of the U.S. Govt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2301 UK Apr RICS Residential Market Survey\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350 JPN Apr Provisional Trade Statistics for 1st 20 days of Month\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350 JPN Apr International Transactions in Securities\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350 JPN Mar Balance of Payments\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350 JPN Apr Bank Lending\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350 JPN Bank of Japan's Summary of Opinions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 10, 2016 17:31 ET (21:31 GMT)\f28 \par 