\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Trading: Japan Warns of Action to Halt Yen Rise -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi   \par \uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2016\par 08:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister said he was "prepared to undertake \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the yen rose further and sharply, describing more explicitly than before a policy the U.S. opposes.\par \par \uc2 The comment by \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  in parliament on Monday was his first direct reference to the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during his tenure as finance minister under Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Aso's remarks added to signs of tension between the U.S. and Japan over exchange rates as both countries struggle to gain traction in the face of slowing global growth. Gains in the yen are generally a blow to Japan's exporters, making them less competitive than their rivals in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The comments helped push the dollar up about 1.2% against the yen to Yen108.38 in late afternoon New York trading, paring part of the dollar's 11% fall against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year through Friday.\par \par \uc2 The finance minister also broke from the protocol of keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  negotiations between countries under wraps to avoid feeding undue speculation. Mr. Aso disclosed how \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  have been at odds in private conversations over the yen's recent appreciation.\par \par \uc2 "As far as I can recall, on one occasion the yen strengthened by about Yen5 [against the dollar] in two days. That was a little excessive," Mr. Aso said as he explained recent market conditions.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  officials think differently, Mr. Aso said. "Their stance is that it [the rise in the yen] is still only Yen5, and we are not at a stage yet" to worry about \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Aso said. "We have often been arguing over the phone."\par \par \uc2 In its semiannual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report issued at the end of April, the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  placed Japan on a list of trading partners whose exchange-rate policies need monitoring. Japan has met two of the three criteria used by the department to identify a country pursuing policy that "could give it an unfair competitive advantage" against the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Investors interpreted Japan's inclusion in the list as a U.S. call against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Mr. Aso said it was due to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade surplus and didn't mean the U.S. found Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy inappropriate.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Aso said the recent volatility in the yen was "not desirable" because it affects all government policy, from trade to economics to fiscal measures. "We are certainly prepared to undertake \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " if the yen continues to make sharp movements, Mr. Aso said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an attempt by authorities to control exchange rates by trading their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in open markets. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fall of 2011, when the dollar was around 75 yen. It currently is about Yen107.50.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Aso also said the Treasury's move to put Japan on a monitoring list "won't constrain" Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Deputy Governor \uc2 Kikuo Iwata\uc2 , also speaking in parliament, said the Treasury report wouldn't affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 10, 2016 02:32 ET (06:32 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160510ec5a000ik\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
