\par\par \b \uc2 Peaceful Presidential Polls Propel Philippines Shares -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2016\par 06:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0444 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Philippines shares are starting to rebound, with fund managers taking advantage of low stock prices in the wake of peaceful presidential elections. "The mandate is clear and the elections were peaceful," said Erwin Balita, a fund manager at BPI Asset Management. The benchmark PSEi rises 0.5% to 7023.62 on heavy trading volumes. Gainers beat losers, 83 to 77. Advancers are led by SM Prime (SMPH.PH), up 4.6% to 23.70 pesos, Ayala Land (ALI.PH), up 0.6% to 34.05 pesos and \uc2 SM Investments\uc2  (SM.PH), up 2.0% to 931.50 pesos. Traders expect the PSEi to move within the 6900-7100 in the near-term. (cris.larano@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0441 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Shares of \uc2 Lenovo Group\uc2  plunged 6.8% in Hong Kong after a downgrade by \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  of the firm's stock. The firm's price target for the stock is now HK$4.2 per share, compared to HK$5.31, where Lenovo now trades. Lenovo is struggling to turn around its smartphone business. In the broader market, shares in Hong Kong pared losses in the morning amid data showing that Chinese inflation rose 2.3% on year in April. The consumer price index rate was steady for the third straight month in a row and slightly undershot market expectations for a 2.4% gain. The Hang Seng Index was last roughly flat. Analysts said that they expect inflationary pressures to remain however, largely driven by food prices and rental inflation and that they expected future policy easing to be more cautious. Trading was cautious in the region with a sharp pullback in oil prices, pushing down energy stocks, including in Hong Kong. (chao.deng@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0437 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY will unlikely break above the 110-mark unless incentives appear--such as fresh stimulus by Japanese authorities before the \f28 \uc2 \f2 G-7\f28 \uc2 \f2  summit (scheduled May 26-27 in Japan), says Yuzo Sakai, a manager at Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  & Ueda Harlow. Despite recent dollar strengthening (largely driven by short-covering) that has pushed up the USD/JPY to a two-week high of 108.86 earlier in the Asia session, "I don't have an image for now that the dollar would surpass the 110 line," he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0425 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sells 2.180 trillion yen of 0.1% 10-year bonds with the lowest price at 101.90, yielding minus 0.091%, which was in line with street forecasts. The bid-to-offer ratio worsened from the last auction to 3.44 from 3.89, while the tail was unchanged at 0.05. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0353 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Philippine peso is stronger against the dollar Tuesday, helped by peaceful Philippine presidential elections and remittance inflow during the extended weekend. "This is a relief rally for the peso. Inflows during the three-day weekend because of Monday's elections is also helping the peso," a Manila-based trader said. The USD/PHP opened at 47.20 and quickly slipped to 46.86. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair is currently at 46.91, heavy trading volume. Traders expect the USD/PHP to move within 46.80-47.20 in the near-term. (Cris.Larano@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0344 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's state-owned enterprise (SOE) liabilities, at more than 115% of GDP in 2015, is a rising risk to the Chinese government, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The rating agency says the government could become responsible for some of the related contingent liabilities should SOEs prove unable to honor their obligations. The portion of SOE liabilities that could potentially require restructuring amounts to 20%-%25% of China's GDP, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It bases this estimate on the cost of equity injections to lower the leverage of the 10% most leveraged SOEs to the median leverage ratio of all SOEs. The cost of any restructuring is unlikely to crystallize solely on the government balance sheet. Solutions would likely involve mergers among SOEs, forbearance and other measures involving banks, the downsizing of some SOEs, equity injections, and other government support, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0333 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's top policymakers seem to hold different views on the domestic economy, adding to uncertainties in policy directions, economists of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  say. A People's Daily article which carried remarks of an unnamed official implies that China will likely become more cautious on monetary and credit easing, Jianguang Shen and Weizhou Yang say in a note. An unnamed "authoritative person" interviewed by the People's Daily said the first-quarter growth was hardly satisfactory as it was investment driven. The mysterious person also called for a "radical reform agenda", such as shutting down firms in sectors with excess capacity and those defaulting on their bonds, the economists say. Other senior officials, including a vice premier and a top economic planner, have cheered the economic performance at the beginning of the year, calling it a "good start". (liyan.qi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0325 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The lowest accepted price for today's 10-year JGB auction is likely to come in around 101.90, traders say. The result is due at 0345 GMT. The latest issue, amounting to 2.4 trillion yen and carrying a coupon of 0.1%, is unchanged from the previous issue. Ahead of the auction results, the benchmark 10-year JGB is yielding minus 0.095%. While bond market analysts expect the auction to have been uneventful they recommend dip buying nonetheless. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0319 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects Chinese corporate onshore green bond issuance to rise once \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's National Association of Financial Market Institutional Investors\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NAFMII) releases regulations for Chinese corporate green bond issuance in the coming months. After these corporate guidelines are released, local government or "municipal" green bond guidance could be next, leading to Chinese onshore green bond muni issuance, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . So far, China's onshore green bonds were mainly issued by banks. Green bonds, which fund environmentally friendly projects, are a fast-growing corner of the fixed-income market. According to \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , global green bond issuance year-to-date amounted US$18.9 billion, up 92% from the same period last year, and is on track to meet \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's US$55-80 billion estimation for 2016. As at end-April, yuan-denominated green bonds accounted for about 5.5% of outstanding global green bonds, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0300 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Consumer inflationary pressure in China will linger, largely driven by food prices and rental inflation, say economists at Nomura. China's headline CPI remained unchanged at 2.3% for the third month in a row in April, well below the government's annual target of 3%, according to official data. Nomura economists also say that PPI deflation may continue to narrow, after the PPI declined 3.4% on year last month compared with a 4.3% fall in March. "Combined with rising financial imbalances, we see future policy easing to be more cautious," say the economists in a note. They add that the debt-fuelled rebound in investment growth will be short-lived, and maintain their forecast of real GDP growth slowing to 6.2% in 2016. (grace.zhu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0258 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Philippine shares are down early Tuesday as the market digests the outcome of Monday's elections. Stocks have been in retreat since mid-April when presumptive presidential race winner, Davao City Mayor Rodrigo Duterte, emerged as leader in pre-election survey. Early vote count shows him with a wide margin. The benchmark PSEi is down 0.3% to 6967.88 in moderate volume. "Investors are still waiting for a pronouncement from Mayor Duterte on who his economic team will be and his economic program," said Astro del Castillo, managing director of First Grade Holdings. He said the market is also preoccupied with the vice presidential race now being contested by administration candidate Congresswoman Leni Robredo and Senator Ferdinand Marcos Jr, son of the former dictator, who was overthrown in the 1986 EDSA Revolution. Losers are beating gainers, 87 to 61. Decliners are led by food company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Universal Robina\f28 \uc2 \f2  (URC.PH), down 1.2% to PHP202, telecom heavyweight PLDT (TEL.PH), down 2.1% to PHP1,625 and conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ayala Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (AC.PH), down 1.3% to PHP725.50. Traders expect bargain-hunting to kick in as the PSEi slides to its immediate support at 6900. (Cris.Larano@WSJ.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0256 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japan's finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taro Aso\f28 \uc2 \f2  has begun to use the term "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in his \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  commentary, in a move that harkens back to Tokyo's forays into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in 2010. On Sept. 15, 2010, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance ministry\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in more than six years in order to knock the yen lower. It dumped about Y2 trillion worth of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the dollar in an open market in a single day, spurning U.S. opposition to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . A week ahead of the action, then-finance minister Yoshihiko Noda started to directly refer to the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on public occasions. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would take "decisive steps" against the yen if necessary, and those steps "naturally include \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Noda said on Sept. 8, 2010. Currently, the chance of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may seem slimmer because of stronger U.S. opposition to any attempts to artificially influence the yen's levels, but the 2010 episode suggests the possibility that action can't be entirely ruled out. (Takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 10, 2016 00:44 ET (04:44 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160510ec5a000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
