\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2016\par 13:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Fed Should Aim for Inflation Overshoot, Says Evans\par \par \uc2 Top Federal Reserve official \uc2 Charles Evans\uc2  said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should consider allowing inflation to temporarily rise above its 2% annual target.\par \par \uc2 Global Stocks Edge Higher on Rising Oil Prices\par \par \uc2 Global stocks mostly inched higher, as investors focused their attention on rising oil prices and Friday's U.S. jobs report.\par \par \uc2 Oil Prices Rise Amid Saudi Uncertainty\par \par \uc2 Crude prices rose on strong Chinese import data and wildfires raging in Canada's oil-producing region, amid uncertainty over Saudi Arabia's unexpected removal of its oil minister.\par \par \uc2 ECB\uc2  Says It Needs to Allow Time for March Measures to Take Hold\par \par \uc2 ECB\uc2  till has policy tools it can use to bring inflation back to its near 2% target, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice president said. He added, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to allow time for the package of measures agreed in March to take hold, suggesting that it is unlikely to change policy soon.\par \par \uc2 IMF Urges Germany to Speed Up Structural Reforms, Raise Investment\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  urged Germany to step up investment and accelerate structural reforms to boost its growth prospects and alleviate the negative effects of a rapidly aging society.\par \par \uc2 Weak Demand Dents China Exports\par \par \uc2 China's exports unexpectedly fell in April, though the results were an improvement over the first quarter.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Threatens \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister said he is "prepared to undertake \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the yen rises more and sharply, countering speculation that U.S. opposition would constrain Tokyo's actions.\par \par \uc2 BOJ Minutes Underscore Split Views on Negative Rates\par \par \uc2 Some \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  officials expressed worries over signs of "adverse effects" of negative interest rates at their March policy meeting, underlining a sharp split among central bankers over the policy measure.\par \par \uc2 Greek Lawmakers Pass Austerity Measures\par \par \uc2 Greece's government hopes the approval of pension changes and tax increases will unlock bailout funds, but its key creditors remain deadlocked over the terms of the country's bailout plan.\par \par \uc2 German Leadership Differs on Greek Debt Relief\par \par \uc2 German Vice Chancellor Sigmar Gabriel said that Greece's debt burden needed to be reduced, signaling a clash inside the \uc2 German government\uc2  as key decisions loom for Athens's creditors.\par \par \uc2 Thousands Rally in Poland to Protest Government\par \par \uc2 Poland's main opposition parties rallied thousands of people in a protest against the country's socially conservative government and its policies they say antagonize key European partners.\par \par \uc2 Italy to Appoint Carlo Calenda as Industry Minister\par \par \uc2 Carlo Calenda, Rome's top European Union representative, will be appointed later this week to replace Federica Guidi, who resigned two months ago over allegations of conflict of interest.\par \par \uc2 Iran Test-Fires Another Ballistic Missile\par \par \uc2 Iran has apparently test-fired a missile with a range of 1,250 miles, the latest in a spate of tests following the implementation of the nuclear deal with world powers.\par \par \uc2 PBOC\uc2  to Offer 'Neutral, Appropriate' Monetary Support For Reform\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would create a monetary environment that is "neutral and appropriate" for the country's structural reform.\par \par \uc2 Japan Wage Growth Picks Up Speed in March\par \par \uc2 Overall cash wages for Japanese workers rose at the fastest pace in nearly two years in March, driven by a jump in bonus payments.\par \par \uc2 Islamic State\uc2  Affiliate Claims Cairo Drive-By Killings\par \par \uc2 Islamic State\uc2  Egypt claimed responsibility for a drive-by shooting that killed eight policemen in a Cairo suburb, the first attack on the capital's police forces in months.\par \par \uc2 Baghdad Attacks Kill at Least 15\par \par \uc2 Multiple attacks in Baghdad killed at least 15 people and wounded scores more, a stark reminder of Iraq's continuing instability amid a political crisis that is heaping pressure on Prime Minister Haider al-Abadi.\par \par \uc2 Landslide in Southern China Leaves 33 Missing\par \par \uc2 Rescuers searched for 33 construction workers missing in a landslide at the site of a hydropower project following days of heavy rain in southern China. Eight other workers were pulled out alive, officials and state-run media reported.\par \par \uc2 Australia to Hold National Election in July\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2  called a July 2 poll, seeking a fresh mandate for the conservative government he took the helm of nearly eight months ago in an economy roiled by voter angst at the end of a long resources boom.\par \par \uc2 Container Ships Collide Off China\par \par \uc2 Two European-owned container ships collided off the coast of China late Saturday with one catching fire, but the crews of both vessels are safe, one of the operators involved said Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  May Cut Rates Further\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on track to lower interest rates again in the coming months as it tries to ward off the risk of a period of prolonged deflation, economists said.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 09, 2016 07:47 ET (11:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160509ec59001il\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
