\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For May 9\b0\par\par\uc2 871 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2016\par 08:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME: \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Directly Refers to Possibility of Yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for First Time \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Monday that he is "prepared to undertake \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the yen rises further and sharply, spurning speculation that U.S. opposition would constrain Tokyo's actions. (published 0343 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par India Passenger-Vehicle Sales Rose 11% in April \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Passenger-vehicle sales in India grew 11% from a year earlier in April thanks to demand for new models and discounts from manufacturers. (published 0515 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China to Offer 'Neutral, Appropriate' Monetary Support for Reform - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would create a monetary environment that is "neutral and appropriate" for the country's structural reform. (published 0201 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ Minutes Underscore Split Views on Negative Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials expressed worries over signs of "adverse effects" of negative interest rates at their March policy meeting, underlining a sharp split among central bankers over the policy measure. (published 0044 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Wage Growth Picks Up Speed in March \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overall cash wages for Japanese workers rose at the fastest pace in nearly two years in March, driven by a jump in bonus payments. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yuexiu Property\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Unit Plans to Issue up to CNY8 Billion Corporate Bonds in China \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese real estate developer Yuexiu Property Co. Ltd. said Monday its unit Guangzhou City Construction & Development Co. plans to issue up to 8 billion yuan of corporate bonds in China. (published 0441 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  of China Selling 3-Year USD-Denominated Bonds via New York Branch -- Term Sheet \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to sell three-year, U.S.-dollar-denominated senior unsecured bonds via its New York branch for general corporate purposes, according to a term sheet seen Monday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0146 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oxley Holdings Plans to Raise S$150 Million Selling Four-Year Bonds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oxley Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it plans to sell 150 million Singapore dollars worth of four-year bonds that will carry a coupon of 5.15% per annum. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Culturecom Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Buy Super Sports Media Inc. for up to HK$3.88 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Culturecom Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has agreed to buy a sports content distributor and broadcaster for up to 3.88 billion Hong Kong dollars . (published 0224 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Heavy Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Undergo More Restructuring, Job Cuts \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Heavy Industries Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will conduct another round of restructuring, including significant job cuts, as the Korean shipyard struggles with slumping ship orders. (published 0216 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HC International\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Sell Beijing Zhixing Ruijing Technology for CNY2.08 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HC International Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has agreed to sell its unit, Beijing Zhixing Ruijing Technology Co., to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Ganglian E-Commerce Holdings Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for 2.08 billion yuan . (published 0131 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Glencore\f28 \uc2 \f2  Becomes Substantial Holder of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Atlas Iron\f28 \uc2 \f2  Stock \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Glencore PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has become a substantial holder of shares in Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Atlas Iron Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., according to a regulatory filing. (published 0130 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Four Seas Mercantile Expects 60%-70% Drop in Profit for Year Ended March \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Four Seas Mercantile Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects to report a 60%-70% decline in profit for the full year ended March. (published 0037 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Hong Kong Food Investment Expects to Swing to Loss for Year Ended March \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Food Investment Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expected to swing to a loss for the year ended March from a net profit of 21.6 million Hong Kong dollars a year earlier. (published 0017 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vallianz Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Signed Charter Contract Worth US$63 Mln With Middle-East Oil Firm for Two Vessels \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vallianz Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it has signed a charter contract worth US$63 million with a state-owned oil company in the Middle East. (published 0010 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Evergrande Real Estate\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Sell 9.96% Stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shengjing Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  For HK$6.93 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Real-estate company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Evergrande Real Estate Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . agreed to sell a 9.96% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shengjing Bank Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for 6.93 billion Hong Kong dollars. (published 0005 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Asian Shares: China Stocks Fall on Concerns Over 'L-Shaped' Economic Trend \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock markets in China were broadly lower Monday, after the Communist Party's mouthpiece reported that the nation's economy is headed for an "L-shaped" recovery, stoking worries among investors that growth in the world's second-largest economy will moderate further. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Prices Jump on Strong China Crude Imports \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil prices climbed higher in early Asian trade Monday as the market honed in on China's strong crude imports last month despite Saudi Arabia's unexpected removal of its long-serving oil minister Ali al-Naimi. (published 0047 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Iron Ore, Steel Rebar Prices Plunge on Expectations of New Speculative-Trading Curbs \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iron ore and steel-rebar futures tumbled in China on Monday on expectations of fresh curbs on speculative trading and weak China trade data. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 09, 2016 02:19 ET (06:19 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160509ec59000g5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
