\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,053 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2016\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ Minutes Underscore Split Views on Negative Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials expressed worries over signs of "adverse effects" of negative interest rates at their March policy meeting, underlining a sharp split among central bankers over the policy measure. (published 0044 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Japan Wage Growth Picks Up Speed in March \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overall cash wages for Japanese workers rose at the fastest pace in nearly two years in March, driven by a jump in bonus payments. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par China's Exports Down 1.8% in April in Dollar Terms \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's exports fell in dollar terms in April from a year earlier, as global demand for goods from the world's second-largest economy remained weak. (published 0240 GMT Sunday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Oxley Holdings Plans to Raise S$150 Million Selling Four-Year Bonds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oxley Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it plans to sell 150 million Singapore dollars worth of four-year bonds that will carry a coupon of 5.15% per annum. (published 0015 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Saudi Arabia Forges Ahead With Change \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia forged ahead a far-reaching government shake-up this weekend, adding to a barrage of proposals aimed at overhauling the economy and convincing legions of young people that change is coming to the conservative kingdom. (published 2338 GMT Sunday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Greece Passes Austerity Measures As Creditors Remain Deadlocked Over Bailout Terms \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's parliament voted to overhaul pensions and increase taxes on Sunday amid strikes and street protests, in a move the government hopes will impress the country's creditors and unlock bailout funds. (published 2214 GMT Sunday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Set to Hold Fast on Policy Following Saudi Oil Minister's Exit -- 2nd Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dismissal of Ali al-Naimi as Saudi Arabia's oil minister puts the country's deputy crown prince firmly in control of energy policy and makes an agreement to freeze oil production less likely when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\f28 \uc2 \f2  meets next month, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials said. (published 1601 GMT Sunday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par Windfall for Central Banks Fuels Political Pressure -- The Outlook \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The financial crisis has been a cash cow for central bankers. They are turning record profits, bolstered by income from their bulging asset and loan portfolios and, more recently, from charging banks for making deposits. (published 1651 GMT Sunday) \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 8 May 2016 23:00 ET \par News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China to Offer 'Neutral, Appropriate' Monetary Support for Reform - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would create a monetary environment that is "neutral and appropriate" for the country's structural reform. (published 0201 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ Minutes Underscore Split Views on Negative Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials expressed worries over signs of "adverse effects" of negative interest rates at their March policy meeting, underlining a sharp split among central bankers over the policy measure. (published 0044 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Japan Wage Growth Picks Up Speed in March \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overall cash wages for Japanese workers rose at the fastest pace in nearly two years in March, driven by a jump in bonus payments. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  of China Selling 3-Year USD-Denominated Bonds via New York Branch -- Term Sheet \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to sell three-year, U.S.-dollar-denominated senior unsecured bonds via its New York branch for general corporate purposes, according to a term sheet seen Monday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0146 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Oxley Holdings Plans to Raise S$150 Million Selling Four-Year Bonds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oxley Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it plans to sell 150 million Singapore dollars worth of four-year bonds that will carry a coupon of 5.15% per annum. (published 0015 GMT) \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 9 May 2016 02:06 ET \par News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Directly Refers to Possibility of Yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for First Time \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Monday that he is "prepared to undertake \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the yen rises further and sharply, spurning speculation that U.S. opposition would constrain Tokyo's actions. (published 0343 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par India Passenger-Vehicle Sales Rose 11% in April \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Passenger-vehicle sales in India grew 11% from a year earlier in April thanks to demand for new models and discounts from manufacturers. (published 0515 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par China to Offer 'Neutral, Appropriate' Monetary Support for Reform - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would create a monetary environment that is "neutral and appropriate" for the country's structural reform. (published 0201 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ Minutes Underscore Split Views on Negative Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials expressed worries over signs of "adverse effects" of negative interest rates at their March policy meeting, underlining a sharp split among central bankers over the policy measure. (published 0044 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Japan Wage Growth Picks Up Speed in March \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overall cash wages for Japanese workers rose at the fastest pace in nearly two years in March, driven by a jump in bonus payments. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yuexiu Property\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Unit Plans to Issue up to CNY8 Billion Corporate Bonds in China \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese real estate developer Yuexiu Property Co. Ltd. said Monday its unit Guangzhou City Construction & Development Co. plans to issue up to 8 billion yuan of corporate bonds in China. (published 0441 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  of China Selling 3-Year USD-Denominated Bonds via New York Branch -- Term Sheet \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to sell three-year, U.S.-dollar-denominated senior unsecured bonds via its New York branch for general corporate purposes, according to a term sheet seen Monday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0146 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Oxley Holdings Plans to Raise S$150 Million Selling Four-Year Bonds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oxley Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it plans to sell 150 million Singapore dollars worth of four-year bonds that will carry a coupon of 5.15% per annum. (published 0015 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Asian Shares: China Stocks Fall on Concerns Over 'L-Shaped' Economic Trend \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock markets in China were broadly lower Monday, after the Communist Party's mouthpiece reported that the nation's economy is headed for an "L-shaped" recovery, stoking worries among investors that growth in the world's second-largest economy will moderate further. (published 0356 GMT) \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 09, 2016 02:06 ET (06:06 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160509ec5900039\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
