\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slips from 18-month high vs dollar, pauses after rally\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2016\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Yen down from Tuesday's 18-month high vs dollar\par \par \uc2 * Short-covering seen helping support dollar/yen\par \par \uc2 * Dollar index pulls away from Tuesday's 15-month low\par \par \uc2 By Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 4 (Reuters) - The yen slipped from an 18-month high against the dollar on Wednesday, losing some steam as position squaring set in after its sharp rally since last week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.6 percent to 107.22 yen, pulling away from Tuesday's low of 105.55 yen, the dollar's weakest level since October 2014.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's gains against the yen came in thin market conditions, with Japanese markets closed on Wednesday and Thursday for public holidays.\par \par \uc2 The dollar could see some whippy trading against the yen over the next couple of days until Tokyo market players return from their holidays, said Satoshi Okagawa, senior global markets analyst for Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "We could see some pretty high volatility," Okagawa said, adding that the greenback could see swings in the 107.50 yen to 105.55 yen area in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Market participants attributed the yen's pullback to position squaring in the wake of its sharp recent rally.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the yen saw its biggest weekly gain since 2008 - more than 5 percent against the dollar - as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  held off from expanding its stimulus.\par \par \uc2 The yen has also gained ground as market participants harbour doubts as to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the yen's gains given wider opposition to such moves globally.\par \par \uc2 In a report last week, the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  called current dollar-yen conditions "orderly" - widely interpreted as a signal to Japanese officials not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 Position squaring ahead of U.S. jobs data later in the week is probably supporting the dollar against the yen for now, said Stephen Innes, senior trader for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker OANDA in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "There's a huge, huge short position built into dollar/yen right now," Innes said.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  data shows that speculators held a net long position in the yen totalling 66,498 contracts in the week ended April 26. That was near the previous week's 71,870 contracts, which was the most bullish positioning in the yen since Reuters records began in March 1995.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was generally firmer after rebounding from lows set on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar edged up 0.2 percent to 93.168. On Tuesday, the dollar index had hit a low of 91.919, its weakest level since January 2015.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.1 percent to about $1.1484, pulling away from Tuesday's high of $1.1616, its strongest level since August.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar regained some ground after it hit a seven-week low of $0.7467 earlier on Wednesday. The Australian dollar last traded at $0.7504, up 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie had tumbled nearly 2.4 percent on Tuesday after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates for the first time in a year, and as commodity prices fell.\par \par \uc2 Later on Wednesday, the focus will be on U.S. economic indicators such as a report on private employment and an industry report on the U.S. services sector. (Editing by Sam Holmes and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-4T05:46:17.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160504ec5400a6p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
