\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia Stocks Close at 3-Month Low; 1MDB Payments Loom -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2016\par 11:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 0953 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The FTSE \uc2 Bursa Malaysia\uc2  Index ends Thursday at a three-month low amid weaker regional markets dragged by lack of fresh stimulus by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 . This is not helped by the persistent cautious market sentiment with state investment fund \uc2 1Malaysia Development Bhd\uc2  (1MDB) debt issue, especially ahead of a looming deadline for guarantor \uc2 International Petroleum Investment Company\uc2  to honor a US$50 million interest payment. In addition, there is another interest payment of US$52.4 million due on May 11 on a separate 1MDB bond. The 30-stocks benchmark index ends the day 1.04% lower at 1,674.76 points, its lowest since January 27.\par \par \uc2  The top losers in the index are cigarette maker \uc2 British American Tobacco (Malaysia) (\uc2 4162.KU) and oil and gas services firm \uc2 SapuraKencana Petroleum\uc2  (5218.KU). The handful of gainers include financial institution \uc2 Hong Leong Financial Group\uc2  (1082.KU) and conglomerate \uc2 PPB Group\uc2  (4065.KU). (yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com; @yantoultra) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0948 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Thai government's push for growth in private consumption cones as the national economy continues to grow at a slower-than-expected pace. The country's private consumption growth is expected to rise to 1.5% in March, compared with a 3.1% year-on-year increase in February. "The positive effects from the junta government's stimulus measures at the end of 2015 have dissipated. Consumer confidence remains weak because of the uncertainty stemming from the upcoming constitutional referendum," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in a note. "Until the political situation is resolved and income growth improves, Thai consumption will remain weak." (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @nopbkk) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0946 GMT Initial claims for unemployment benefits hit a seasonally adjusted 247,000 in the week ended April 16, their lowest level since November 1973. But don't count on another record being set this morning. Economists surveyed by WSJ expect the Labor Department will report initial jobless claims of 257,000 for the week ended April 23, up from the prior week but still at low levels consistent with a healthy U.S. job market. It would be the 60th consecutive week that claims remained below 300,000, extending the longest streak since 1973. (Ben.Leubsdorf@wsj.com, @BenLeubsdorf) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0945 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 America Movil\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be suffering from competition in Mexico and heavy exposure to Latin America, but its geographic diversification, thanks to its stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekom Austria\f28 \uc2 \f2 , reassures \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kepler Cheuvreux\f28 \uc2 \f2  credit research. The brokerage keeps its hold recommendation. It also likes the management's commitment to a single-A rating. The Mexican telecom has a series of benchmark-size euro-denominated bonds outstanding. The shortest one, a EUR1 billion 3.75% issue, is scheduled to mature in late June 2017. The longest bullet bond goes all the way to 2028. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0942 GMT Strong U.S. data could see the dollar rise if the market starts to think a June rate hike by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is possible, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. So far the dollar has traded softer in response to the Fed leaving market expectations intact that a hike in June is possible but not too likely. "As hardly anyone expected a rate step in June anyway the reaction of the dollar is muted at present," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. However, if data over coming weeks is "surprisingly positive" this could cause the Fed to signal a hike in June, risking a "strong rise in the dollar." (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0939 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Roughly two weeks since The Wall Street Journal grilled Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda in an interview about the need for "helicopter money," the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief found himself fielding similar questions at a regular news conference. The development illustrates growing skepticism toward his policy and his ability to take the Japanese to a land he has promised, where prices rise steadily at an annual pace of 2% and the economy grows strongly (prices are falling and the economy is teetering on the edge of recession.) But Kuroda, a renowned champion of budgetary overhauls, brushed aside the question. It isn't a good idea to mix up responsibilities of fiscal and monetary authorities, and, more important, Japan's law rules out monetization, he says. (Takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0935 GMT Regional data from six German states suggest that Germany's nationwide annual HICP inflation fell back to zero in April, while core inflation remained very weak, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jennifer McKeown\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior European economist at Capital Economics. This adds pressure on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to do more to reach its inflation target, she adds. Economists polled in a Wall Street Journal survey expect HICP at -0.3% month on month and at 0.0% year on year. The inflation figures are due at 1200 GMT. (emese.bartha@wsj.com ; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0933 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  inaction has rekindled views it is wary of U.S. and European criticism that Tokyo cheapens the yen for trade advantage. "It is possible that BOJ policy has been affected by warnings from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of 20\f28 \uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says Dai-ichi Life Research Institute chief economist Hideo Kumano. "That makes it quite challenging to forecast additional easing." Such speculation may be hard to squash. Japan this year is chair of the smaller but ultimately more important \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of Seven\f28 \uc2 \f2  leading industrialized nations. Plausibly, it is wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the markets just ahead of this gathering, exposing it to criticism from this influential group. The BOJ's decision Thursday sent the yen soaring and Japan stocks tanking. (Takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0928 GMT Tourism is a key sector of the Turkish economy, and thus important for the balance of payments--a net earner of something like 3-3.5% of GDP, says Tim Ash, an economist at Nomura. Turkey's foreign tourists arrivals dropped 12.8% on the year in March to 1.65 million after Russia's tourism ban. "Plus add in there concerns on the security front, after recent terrorism and the concern is that a perfect storm is building for the sector, which could feed into real estate/construction and then back to banks," he adds. (yeliz.candemir@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0928 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Jakarta Composite Index holds on to a positive performance despite losses in other Asian markets, Thursday, ending the day up 0.1% at 4848.39. The broad direction of trade was driven by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decisions in both the U.S. and Japan. The Fed stood pat, which was in line with expectations, while the BOJ surprised markets by also making no policy moves, which drove Japanese stocks sharply lower and took some other Asian markets with it. In local markets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Media Nusantara Citra\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MNCN.JK) leads gainers, up 3.9%, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Surya Citra Media\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SCMA.JK) rises 3.6%. Telecommunications stock are the worst performers, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 XL Axiata\f28 \uc2 \f2  (EXCL.JK) down 3.9% on earnings and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telekomunikasi Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (TLKM.JK) falling 2.8%. (jake.watts@wsj.com; @jmwatts_) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0926 GMT SKF's decision to sell the Kaydon velocity control business to Stabilus is positive for the Swedish company as proceeds are expected to go toward trimming the debt burden, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The sale should improve SKF's debt-to-Ebitda ratio to around 3.4 times from 3.6 times in the 12 months to December 2015. Analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Martin Fujerik\f28 \uc2 \f2  says "the fairly high leverage is the major constraint" on SKF's rating. While SKF has room to cut down on its asset portfolio even further, Mr. Fujerik doesn't expect any major sales. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0924 GMT The Russian ruble's period of sharp depreciation is over, as Russia's balance of payments suggests, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It revises its ruble forecast and now sees USD/RUB at 70 rubles with an oil prices of $40 per barrel by the end of the year versus 80 rubles expected previously. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  sticks to its prediction that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't lower the key rate this year due to domestic budget-related risks and external risks, such as possibility of a rate hike by U.S. Fed.(andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 28, 2016 05:53 ET (09:53 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160428ec4s001lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
