\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Tumbles on Speculation of New Stimulus -- Update -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chelsey Dulaney   \par \uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2016\par 23:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The yen fell to a three-week low against the dollar on Friday amid speculation that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will introduce new stimulus at its meeting next week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 2% to Yen111.635, while the euro rose 1.4% to Yen125.32.\par \par \uc2 The yen had rallied this month to its strongest point against the dollar since October 2014, driven in part by speculation that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Speculative investors pushed bullish bets on the yen to a record high in the week ended April 12, according to regulatory data.\par \par \uc2 But reports Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could expand the negative interest-rate policy it put in place in January sparked profit-taking among some investors, according to Win Thin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Brown Brothers Harriman Co. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scheduled to meet April 27 and 28.\par \par \uc2 "People are nervous already going into the BOJ meeting next week," Mr. Thin said. "These reports that they may have something cooking...[and] have spooked some people."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar rose against many of its peers as investors grapple with the prospect that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  could raise interest rates sooner than expected. While few expect the Fed to change interest rates at its meeting next week, some investors think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take a more upbeat outlook on the economy, which could fuel expectations for a June rate increase.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index, which measures the buck against a basket of 16 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose 0.6% to 86.70. The euro fell 0.5% to $1.1229.\par \par \uc2 Write to Chelsey Dulaney at Chelsey.Dulaney@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 22-04-16 2120GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160422ec4m000hz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
