\par\par \b \uc2 China's Yuan Fixing Gains 0.19% Against US Dollar -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2016\par 03:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0129 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the yuan's daily mid-point rate at 6.4787 from Friday's rate of 6.4908 against the dollar, representing a 0.19% strengthening of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The downwards adjustment of the USD/CNY benchmark rate appears to coincide with Friday's drop of the ICE U.S. dollar index, which measures the value of the U.S. dollar against six other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Aside from the nudge higher by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan could also rally in the spot market due to spillover gains from the Japanese yen. The yen is a factor in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -valuation basket used by the authorities to manage the yuan, so when peer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate, the yuan ought to as well. The Japanese yen has strengthened after an apparent failure to win approval from G20 leaders over the weekend to employ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. The strength of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a bane for the nation's export-led economic growth. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: JFN\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 18-04-16 0144GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160418ec4i0002g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
