\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary: Despite Japanese Yen Appreciation,  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Market Orderly\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2016\par 00:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 15 Apr 2016 18:17 ET *\uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary: Japan Recommitted to \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Commitments\par \par \uc2 15 Apr 2016 18:17 ET *\uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary's Comments Come Amid Concerns Japan May Depreciate Yen\par \par \uc2 15 Apr 2016 18:17 ET *\uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary: China's New Economic Policies Address Some Challenges\par \par \uc2 15 Apr 2016 18:17 ET *\uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary: New Chinese Policies Should Help Deal With Excess Capacity\par \par \uc2 15 Apr 2016 19:25 ET  U.S. Treasury Secretary: Despite Yen's Appreciation, \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market Orderly\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Ian Talley \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON -- U.S. Treasury Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacob Lew\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Friday said the Japanese yen's recent appreciation was part of a largely orderly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, comments likely intended to ward off any potential move by Tokyo to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Lew's comments, made after meetings with top Japanese finance officials in Washington, follow rising speculation that authorities may ramp up its monetary stimulus in a bid to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Despite recent yen appreciation, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets remain orderly," Mr. Lew said.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and other global heavyweights, have said they won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in markets unless strong exchange rate movements threaten to jeopardize their economies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier this week, Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said the yen's recent rise has been "excessive," his strongest language yet on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent moves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Kuroda's remarks were seen as likely to fuel speculation the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  might soon ramp up their easy-money policies in a bid to undercut the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It also rekindled speculation Tokyo might resort to radical steps, such as direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. Under its existing commitments, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has argued it and other countries should be allowed to take measures when there is "excessive" volatility or "disorderly" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Lew said his Japanese counterparts "agreed that monetary policy alone cannot lead to balanced growth." He said: "Given the backdrop of weak global growth, Japan needs to look to domestic rather than external demand," a reference to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakening that makes exports more attractive overseas, but at the expense of other nations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The secretary also said Japan, along with members of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of Seven\f28 \uc2 \f2  industrialized economies and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of 20\f28 \uc2 \f2  largest economies, have recommitted to refrain from seeking to gain a competitive trade advantage through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation. G-20 countries earlier this year agreed to "communicate with each other so that there are no surprises and refrain from exchange rate targeting in our policies," a reference to new commitments made in February amid heightened fears of a global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Takashi Nakamichi contributed to this\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ian Talley at ian.talley@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 15, 2016 19:25 ET (23:25 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160416ec4f0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
