\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen up as oil falls\b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2016\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Yen benefits from dip in oil, stock markets\par \par \uc2 * Aussie, kiwi dollars gain on Chinese numbers\par \par \uc2 * Japan's Kuroda, Aso remark on yen's recent rapid moves\par \par \uc2 * Eyes on G20 meetings in Washington, \uc2 ECB\uc2  next week\par \par \uc2 By Patrick Graham\par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 15 (Reuters) - The dollar fell half a percent against the yen on Friday as a pull back in oil prices ahead of weekend talks between producers in Doha capped investors' appetite for risk and sent capital towards the traditional security of Japan.\par \par \uc2 The major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen as most dependent on China were also among those rising after a batch of GDP data offered hope that the world's second largest economy was heading for a rebound after its slowest growth in seven years.\par \par \uc2 The Australian and New Zealand dollars, generally in more bullish form since long-term downtrends bottomed out in January, rose 0.3 and 0.9 percent respectively.\par \par \uc2 The yen was higher across the board, rising to 108.85 yen per dollar and 0.4 percent to 122.77 per euro. It is still well short of highs hit at the start of the week.\par \par \uc2 "There is some profit-taking but I think this market is largely driven by oil," said Stephen Gallo, a strategist with \uc2 BMO\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "More generally, it is a very fickle market at the moment. There's not a lot of conviction or ability to put on clear trending macro trades and we have seen the dollar both rise and fall with improved risk appetite this week."\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks have risen despite generally downbeat expectations for the start of the earnings season and European shares are up for the first week in four. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still up 0.5 percent on the week in trade-weighted terms.\par \par \uc2 It was up 0.2 percent against the euro at $1.1285. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  strategist Thu Lan Nguyen said those gains may be partially the result of expectations of another pro-easing message from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week.\par \par \uc2 "The general theme is a slight recovery of the dollar as well as some euro weakness, which may have to do with people preparing for \uc2 the ECB\uc2  meeting," she said.\par \par \uc2 The run in to a gathering of G20 financial leaders in Washington has been marked by rhetoric from Japanese officials used in the past to prepare markets for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Taro Aso said he had expressed deep concerns to U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew over one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda also said in Washington that the yen's "excessive" rises have been corrected somewhat in the past few days.\par \par \uc2 While it is the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that determines Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, Kuroda's remarks were notable in that it was the first time he described the yen's appreciation as "excessive".\par \par \uc2 Traders in Asia reported that Japanese importers had bought dollars on Friday as a "gotobi" date - a multiple of five - on which books are traditionally settled.\par \par \uc2 "Today is 'gotobi,' so it's natural for the dollar to rise a little bit," said Masashi Murata, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in Tokyo. (Editing by Andrew Heavens and David Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-15T13:09:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160415ec4f00ill\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
