\par\par \b \uc2 USD/JPY Rebounds, but Bears May Be Lurking Near 109.45 -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2016\par 08:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0553 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/JPY has tentatively reclaimed the 108.00 round-figure trading barrier, after Japan's finance minister Taro Aso hinted at the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. There has been contention as to whether the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be called upon to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the geopolitical implications of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, especially ahead of the G7 meeting to be hosted by Japan in May. Aso said that he thinks the G20 group will allow its members to take steps against one-sided, speculative moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The USD/JPY rose as high as 108.30 from an intraday trough of 107.84, and may have room to rally. Short covering could drive the dollar toward 109.45, where the ceiling of the Bollinger downtrend channel awaits. But if the USD/JPY ends Tuesday below that mark, the dollar-bears could return to sell on the spike. The USD/JPY is now at 108.30 from its Monday close of 107.93. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: JFN\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 12-04-16 0610GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160412ec4c0004m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
