\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Weaker Against Rivals After Japan Finance Minster Comments -3-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Hiroyuki Kachi   \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2016\par 07:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The yen was weaker against its rivals during Asia trade Tuesday after the Japanese finance minister's warning against excessive yen strength.\par \par \uc2 Around 0450 GMT, the U.S. dollar was changing hands at Y108.21, higher than Y107.95 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The greenback advanced to an intraday high of Y108.28 during the lunchtime break in Tokyo, extending earlier gains after Finance Minister Taro Aso said the world's leading economies would find it acceptable for a nation to act against "one-sided, speculative" exchange-rate movements.\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heads from the G-20 wealthy and developing economies are scheduled to gather in Washington later this week.\par \par \uc2 But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to test further upside against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as selling set in on the recovery.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar is seeking its direction now" ahead of the G-20 meeting, said Toshihiko Sakai, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial products trading division at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking.\par \par \uc2 Investors will find it difficult to make major moves Tuesday or Wednesday, as it is unclear if the dollar's recent decline will continue or abate after the G-20 meeting, Mr. Sakai said.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo-based dealers and analysts said the yen's recent rise isn't a sign of investors' buying the perceived safety of the yen, but a function of dollar-selling after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  signaled it will move more slowly to raise rates this year.\par \par \uc2 Investors also continue to push up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the expectation the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to blunt the yen's strength out of concern that Tokyo's trade partners would accuse it of manipulating exchange rates to help exports.\par \par \uc2 The yen weakened against the euro. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to Y123.46 from Y123.17 late Monday, while the U.K. pound grew to Y154.16 from Y153.69.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar increased to Y82.66 from Y82.00.\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs, the euro was at $1.1408 from $1.1410.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index, a measure of the dollar against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was down 0.01% at 85.90.\par \par \uc2 Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par USD/JPY Japan           108.22-23      107.94-95  +0.26   108.28   107.88 -10.04 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.1408-11      1.1407-10  +0.01   1.1419   1.1401  +5.06 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.4245-47      1.4238-40  +0.05   1.4248   1.4227  -3.33 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9538-42      0.9540-44  -0.02   0.9555   0.9538  -4.79 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.2891-96     1.2895-900  -0.03   1.2919   1.2890  -6.83 \par AUD/USD Australia       0.7637-41      0.7593-97  +0.58   0.7646   0.7583  +4.83 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.6883-89      0.6857-63  +0.38   0.6893   0.6851  +0.78 \par Euro Rate \par EUR/JPY Japan           123.43-47      123.11-15  +0.26 