\par\par \b \uc2 Japan's Finance Minister Asserts G-20 Allows for 'Necessary' Steps on Cu\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi   \par \uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2016\par 05:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Japan's finance minister ratcheted up his warnings against the rising yen Tuesday, saying the world's leading economies find it acceptable for a nation to act against "one-sided, speculative" exchange-rate movements.\par \par \uc2 The remark by Finance Minister Taro Aso is likely aimed at countering speculation that Tokyo may hold off from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to arrest the yen's strength out of concern that its trade partners would accuse it of manipulating exchange rates to help exports.\par \par \uc2 "As we have been saying, we will, if the situation calls for it, take necessary measures if there are one-sided, speculative movements" in the yen, Mr. Aso said at a regular news conference. "I believe this kind of step is considered acceptable under the agreement of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heads from the G-20 wealthy and developing economies gather in Washington later this week to discuss ways to tackle protracted weakness in global growth.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. and Europe have previously signaled their opposition to both verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making traders doubt Tokyo would directly step into the market to dump yen to force it lower -- a step last taken in 2011. Open complaints from overseas often weaken the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't continue the action for long.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Aso said G-20 representatives need to reaffirm that excessive volatility or disorderly exchange-rate movements in could damage growth.\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 12-04-16 0303GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160412ec4c0002e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
