\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Key Dollar Gauge Falls To Nearly 8-month Low\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2016\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Joseph Adinolfi, \uc2 MarketWatch\uc2  , Hiroyuki Kachi\par \par \uc2 Dollar turns lower against yen, euro and pound and emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded broadly lower on Monday as doubts about the pace of \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  interest-rate hikes weighed on it.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ICE\uc2  U.S. Dollar index , a measure of the dollar's aggregate strength against a basket of six rivals, briefly fell to its lowest level since late August before trimming its decline to finish the day down 0.3% at 93.9200.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said investors are looking for the next \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  interest-rate hike to come after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's June meeting, which is simultaneously weighing on the dollar and driving U.S. stocks higher. A stronger dollar has often been cited as a headwind for the quarterly results of multinational companies.\par \par \uc2 After spending most of the session in the green, U.S. stocks sold off in afternoon trade as investors worried first-quarter corporate earnings might have a weak tone ahead of a report by \uc2 Alcoa, Inc\uc2 .(AA) , expected after the bell. \uc2 Alcoa\uc2 's earnings are widely considered the unofficial start of earnings season. The S&P 500 was down 3.43 points, or 0.2%, to 2,063.01 in recent trade.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar's looking very soft," said Stephen Gallo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BMO Capital Markets\uc2 . "Provided we don't get any negative news that drives the yen higher, we're on the cusp of the weaker dollar being synonymous with risk on."\par \par \uc2 The dollar encountered renewed weakness on the expectation that the Fed would likely only raise interest rates one more time in 2016, if that.\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded at Yen107.91 late Monday in New York, compared with Yen108.09 late Friday in New York. It also fell to a nearly 18-month low during the Asia trading day.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials continued to warn that the government could take action to curb excessive yen strength, with Chief Cabinet Secretary Yoshihide Suga once again blaming speculators for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent resilience. But the comments appeared to have little lasting impact.\par \par \uc2 Despite the jawboning from government officials, many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists remain skeptical that \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the entity in charge of setting yen policy, would condone selling yen in the market.\par \par \uc2 Particularly, there are doubts about the efficacy of a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an unwillingness to open \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to accusations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.\par \par \uc2 "From the market chatter, one could be forgiven for thinking that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is common for Japanese policy makers. Nothing is further from the truth, though \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats are frequently voiced," said Alvin Tan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Early strength in the yen weighed on Japanese stocks, with the Nikkei 225 Stock Average finishing down 70.39 points, or 0.4%, at 15,751.13.\par \par \uc2 Read: \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't be gentle with yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/japan-cant-be-gentle-with-yen-intervention-2016-04-08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/\b  \highlight22japan\b0 \highlight22 -cant-be-gentle-with-yen-\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 -2016-04-08}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, the euro rose to $1.1407 late Monday in New York, compared with $1.1402 late Friday. The pound traded at $1.4243 late Monday, its strongest level in nearly a week, compared with $1.4125 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was also broadly lower compared with its emerging-market rivals. Rising oil prices were seen supporting the Russian ruble , Brazilian real , Mexican peso as well as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other commodity exporters.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 11, 2016 16:18 ET (20:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160411ec4b0038h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
