\par\par \b \uc2 CS Keeps Outperform Rating on \uc2 Fletcher Building\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2016\par 02:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0006 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Given current low expectations, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  thinks \uc2 Fletcher Building\uc2 's (FBU.NZ) stock price should respond positively if management delivers on its guidance and signals further growth in fiscal year 2017 forecasts. Roughly 72% of earnings are sourced from New Zealand, where ongoing strength in the building and construction sector is being led by higher population growth, demand for housing and commercial building activity. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  keeps its Outperform rating on FBU, with an unchanged target price of NZ$9.36. (rachel.pannett@wsj.com; Twitter: @RachelPannett)\par \par \uc2 0002 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  downgrades \uc2 Platinum Asset Management\uc2  (PTM.AU) to underperform from neutral, citing a weak growth outlook and risk that earnings will fall on retail outflows. It also says there's little valuation appeal for investors given the stock is trading at 17.5-times earnings, an 11% premium to its peers. The company "has reported three consecutive months of retail outflows, which are accelerating," it says. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  cautions the company has historically endured "outflow cycles that extend many months" and says it has "little fat in the cost base to cushion earnings" from those outflows. The broker cuts its target to A$6.00 from A$6.50. \uc2 Platinum Asset Management\uc2  last traded at A$6.10/share. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 2358 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Japan's core machinery orders for February, a leading indicator of business investment, fell 9.2% from the previous month, after a 15.0% jump in January. The result was better than a 12.0% fall expected by economists surveyed by The Wall Street Journal and the Nikkei. The Cabinet Office maintained its view that machinery orders are on a recovery trend. (mitsuru.obe@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2357 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Australia's job market will be back in focus on Thursday, with March data due. Any hint of weakness will see already rising bets for an RBA rate cut in May strengthen. In March, unemployment fell to 5.8% from 6.0%, helped by a sharp fall in workforce participation. That drop in participation skewed the data, disguising developing weakness in the job market, some economists argued. But Sally Auld, chief economist at J.P. Morgan, says the participation drop last month was largely limited to males aged 15 to 24. The participation drop was not broad-based. "As such, we view the supply-side weakness as short-term aberration that is likely to be unwound, to an extent, in this week's release," she said. Leading employment indicators continue to portend a strengthening labor market, with job vacancies edging higher and the \uc2 NAB\uc2  employment and capacity utilization measures also solid, she added. Ms. Auld expects a 20,000 gain in employment in March, with unemployment rising to 5.9%. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2354 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Nikkei is likely to hover in a 15,500-16,000 range Monday, with investors keeping their eyes on the JPY performance, says Masahiro Ichikawa, senior strategist at Sumitomo Mitsui Asset Management. Solid gains in U.S. stocks and higher oil prices Friday may provide a support to the benchmark Nikkei, "but it largely depends on the yen's performance," says Ichikawa. A stronger JPY hurts the Japanese corporate sector, especially exporters, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  factor helps scale down USD-denominated revenue and profits earned outside Japan. Nikkei 225 June March futures ended Friday's Chicago trading at 15,775, compared with an earlier close in Osaka at 15,830. In the cash market, the Nikkei was 0.5% higher at 15,821.52 Friday. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2346 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Australian shares are expected to head higher in early trade after rising oil prices boosted U.S. stocks Friday, with the futures market suggesting the \uc2 ASX\uc2  200 will start up around 20 points, or 0.4%. "The rally in the oil price was a positive for equity markets on Friday and Asian markets are looking to move higher today as well," says IG market analyst Angus Nicholson. "The big Aussie miners had a very strong session on the FTSE, which is a good signal for the \uc2 ASX\uc2 , but, of course, for good gains today the under pressure banks will also have to find buyers." Australia's banks have been under pressure in recent weeks amid concerns a stretch of low bad-debt costs will soon turn as commodities prices remain weak and with analyst suggestions the big lenders will again face regulatory pressure to increase capital buffers against the risk of economic shocks. (rebecca.thurlow@wsj.com; @beckthurlow)\par \par \uc2 2339 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The U.S. dollar is set to rise against the yen this week on profit\u8209\'20\'11taking and a pricing of some risk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, says CBA. Japanese officials have ramped up their rhetoric as the yen has strengthened to 18 month highs, it adds. "We do not expect the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels. Even if the BoJ do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , history shows market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically fails after a week or two with pair resuming its prior trend," it adds. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2329 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Australian dollar is vulnerable to a re\u8209\'20\'11pricing in the money market to rate cut risks for the RBA's May 3 policy meeting if the Australian March labor force report on Thursday does not show a strong rebound in employment, says CBA. CBA's economists predict employment to surge by 30,000 after three months of virtually no growth in jobs. Another downside risk to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week is China data for March and 1Q GDP. CBA says the risks to the Chinese economic data this week remain skewed to the downside. The Australian dollar should find support around the 100 day moving average of US$0.7256 should all the downside risks materialize, it adds. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2326 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The proposed change in \uc2 ASX\uc2  (ASX.AU) ownership restrictions, following introduction of regulation regarding clearing market structure and removal of the \uc2 ASX\uc2  monopoly for equity clearing, increases the potential for M&A activity, Macquarie says. \uc2 ASX\uc2  is currently subject to a 15% ownership cap with a positive public interest test. Following proposed clearing market structure changes, the \uc2 ASX\uc2  is expected to have the same ownership restrictions as other financial sector entities, which is 15% and subject to the approval of the Treasurer on a negative national interest test. Still, with activity levels generally subdued, Macquarie keeps an Underperform rating on the stock, with a 12-month price target of A$40.30. \uc2 ASX\uc2  last traded Friday at A$41.49. (rachel.pannett@wsj.com; Twitter: @RachelPannett)\par \par \uc2 2323 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Iluka Resources Ltd\uc2 . (ILU.AU) promises to pay out a minimum of 40% of free cash flow in capital returns to investors. Over the next few years, though, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  thinks the miner--which has a strong balance sheet, but earnings that are being squeezed by a deepening downturn in zircon prices--will hand back 100% of free cash flow in dividends. In FY16, that would equate to a dividend of roughly A$0.39/share, or a yield of 6.7%, it projects. "The trouble is Iluka won't be able to sustain this level of dividend on our modelling and we see the dividend contracting to A$0.25 in FY17," says the broker. It cuts its price target to A$5.50 from A$6.00 and keeps an underperform rating. Iluka last traded at A$5.82. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 2314 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] New Zealand's consumer price index is likely to barely increase in Q1 2016, says \uc2 Jane Turner\uc2 , senior economist at ASB Bank. ASB expects New Zealand's CPI to rise 0.1% quarter-on-quarter and 0.3% year-on-year. "Q1 price trends may be overshadowed by a series of large individual moves that are typically looked though when assessing core inflation, for example petrol, seasonality and taxes. However, beyond taxes and housing we see very little evidence of inflation picking up." ASB expects the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  to cut the official cash rate twice more this year, from its current setting of 2.25%, but Turner says "a slightly weaker CPI result may not necessarily provide the case for urgency." New Zealand's Q1 CPI is due to be released on April 18 and the RBNZ makes its next interest rate decision on April 28. (kate.geenty@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2312 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Consistent output, falling costs and a firm gold-price outlook should allow \uc2 Evolution Mining Ltd\uc2 . (EVN.AU) to continue to pay down its debts ahead of schedule, says \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . The broker says Evolution has done a good job cutting operating costs already and thinks it will be able to further tighten expenses at its new Cowal and Mungari mines, "with increased time" in Evolution's control. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  has an outperform rating and A$1.75 target on the stock, which last traded at A$1.66/share. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 10, 2016 20:06 ET (00:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160411ec4b0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
