\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Rises as Investors Ignore Rhetoric of Japanese Officials -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chelsey Dulaney   \par \uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2016\par 23:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The yen ticked up Friday, heading for its sixth straight day of gains as investors shook off talk by Japanese officials aimed at halting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped about 0.1% to Yen108.1, reversing gains of as much as 0.8% from earlier in the day. The dollar this week has traded at its lowest point against the yen since October 2014.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index, which measures the greenback against 16 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell 0.4% to 86.21 as the dollar fell against all major rivals, including the pound and Canadian dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of commodity-dependent nations rose on soaring oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The yen's rally, driven in part by investor demand for safe-haven assets, highlights concerns about global economic health and the outsize effect of expansive \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  in January introduced negative rates, which should have weakened the yen and made the country's exports more competitive globally. Instead, the yen has been the year's best-performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , threatening Japan's plans to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials recently increased their rhetoric about the yen's rally and have said they could take necessary measures if the yen doesn't weaken. But many strategists bet the yen has further to rise before the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  would make the contentious decision to step in.\par \par \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  strategists said in a report Friday that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the dollar falls to Yen100, a level not seen since 2013.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar fell 1.2% against the Canadian dollar to C$1.2992. The buck fell 1.1% against the Norwegian krone to 8.2299.\par \par \uc2 Write to Chelsey Dulaney at Chelsey.Dulaney@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 08-04-16 2136GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160408ec48000fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
