\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar extends slide vs yen as BOJ seen on hold\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2016\par 21:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Dollar falls to fresh 17-month low of 107.71 yen\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see BOJ unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Euro falls vs dollar after hitting nearly 6-month high\par \par \uc2 * Greenback seen firmly bit by year-end - Reuters poll (Updates prices, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Sam Forgione\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, April 7 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar fell below 108 yen for the first time in 17 months on Thursday on bets the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the euro slipped against the dollar on the potential for a more dovish \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell as much as 1.6 percent against the yen to 107.71 yen, its lowest since late October 2014, before paring some losses in late trading.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ has not signaled it would step in to halt the yen's rally, and investors have been forced to exit long-held short bets against the yen, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "What (investors) are seeing now is that (Japanese) policymakers aren't providing the support for dollar/yen that they would have expected," said Shahab Jalinoos, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York. "That's creating some degree of confusion, and of course, prudent risk management suggests one scales back on short positions."\par \par \uc2 The dollar has fallen nearly 10 percent against the yen for the year, with the past week accounting for roughly 3 percent of the move.\par \par \uc2 BOJ Governor Haruhiko Kuroda said in a quarterly meeting of BOJ branch managers the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to take additional monetary easing steps if needed to hit the bank's 2 percent inflation target.\par \par \uc2 But he also said Japan's economy continues to recover moderately as a trend, and the head of the BOJ's Nagoya branch said Japanese automobile exports remain strong with no big damage seen from the yen's recent rises.\par \par \uc2 The euro weakened against the dollar from $1.1453, its highest level in nearly six months, to a session low of $1.1338. It was last down 0.2 percent at $1.1375.\par \par \uc2 Investors may be preparing for the possibility of more stimulus from \uc2 the ECB\uc2  to counter the euro's recent strength, said Omer Esiner, chief market analyst at \uc2 Commonwealth \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Inc\uc2  in Washington.\par \par \uc2 "(\uc2 The ECB\uc2 ) can't be happy with the euro's performance now close to $1.15," Esiner said. "That may suggest that \uc2 the ECB\uc2  may want to kind of step up its dovishness."\par \par \uc2 The ECB\uc2  targets inflation just below 2 percent, but flash data recently showed it was -0.1 percent in March. In addition, there are few signs \uc2 the ECB\uc2 's latest round of stimulus has had much impact on growth.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index, which measures the greenback against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was last up 0.08 percent at 94.501, from an earlier nearly six-month low of 94.015.\par \par \uc2 However, the greenback is expected to stage modest gains against the euro and yen by the end of the year, according to a Reuters poll released on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sam Forgione; Additional reporting by Patrick Graham in London; Editing by Andrea Ricci and Chris Reese) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-7T20:42:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160407ec4701x29\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\