 Street was lower on Thursday as oil prices\par slid and investors worried that measures taken by central banks\par may not be enough to put the global economy back on track.\par     At 12:40 p.m. ET, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  industrial average \par was down 158.44 points, or 0.89 percent, at 17,557.61, the S&P\par 500 was down 21.19 points, or 1.03 percent, at 2,045.47\par and the Nasdaq Composite was down 58.73 points, or 1.19\par percent, at 4,861.98. \par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     LONDON -  Britain's top share index dipped on Thursday,\par although rises in pharmaceutical stocks and retailers after a\par well-received update from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marks and Spencer\f28 \uc2 \f2  supported UK\par equities.\par     The FTSE 100 was down 24.74 points, or 0.4 percent, at\par 6,136.89 points at its close, outperforming the broader European\par market which extended losses after Wall Street fell.\par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     TOKYO - Japanese stocks edged up on Thursday in choppy\par trade, snapping a seven-day losing streak as buying in defensive\par stocks offset weakness in exporters which lost ground on the\par yen's strength.\par     The Nikkei share average gained 0.2 percent to\par 15,749.84.\par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par     NEW YORK - The U.S. dollar fell below 108 yen for the first\par time in 17 months on Thursday on continued expectations the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while the euro fell against\par the dollar on the potential for a more dovish \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The dollar fell more than 1.6 percent against the yen \par to 107.94 yen, its lowest level since late October 2014.\par Analysts said the BOJ was not indicating it would step in to\par halt the yen's rally.\par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     TREASURIES \par     NEW YORK - \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields fell broadly on Thursday to\par their lowest levels since late February as declining oil prices\par and global growth fears underpinned bond prices.\par     Benchmark 10-year Treasuries rose 12/32 in price\par to yield 1.711 percent, their lowest since March 1 and down over\par 3 basis points from late on Wednesday.\par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     COMMODITIES \par     GOLD\par     NEW YORK - Gold jumped almost two percent on Thursday as the\par dollar fell to a 17-month low against the Japanese yen following\par minutes from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's latest meeting and\par global shares fell, rekindling investor appetite for safer\par assets.\par     Spot gold hit a two-week high of $1,243.50 an ounce,\par a rise of 1.8 percent, and was up 1.3 percent at $1,237.60 at\par 2:23 p.m. EDT (1823 GMT). U.S. gold futures for June delivery\par  settled up 1.1 percent at $1,223.80 an ounce. \par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     BASE METALS\par     LONDON - Copper fell 3 percent to its lowest in a month on\par Thursday as concerns over demand from major consumer China\par helped push the metal through key chart support, triggering\par further selling.\par     Three-month copper on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Metal Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par closed at $4,650.50 a tonne, down 2.9 percent.\par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - - \par     OIL\par     NEW YORK - Oil prices fell around 2 percent on Thursday\par after industry data suggested a key pipeline shutdown had not\par reduced crude flows to the U.S. storage base by as much as\par expected. \par     Brent futures were down 85 cents, or 2.1 percent, at\par $38.99 a barrel by 10:41 a.m. EDT (1441 GMT).\par     For a full report, double click on \par     - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-7T20:11:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160407ec4701vld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
