\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Nears 18-month Low Versus Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2016\par 21:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Joseph Adinolfi and Sara Sjolin, \uc2 MarketWatch\uc2  , Hiroyuki Kachi\par \par \uc2 Yen strength shows selloff fears 'haven't entirely gone away'\par \par \uc2 The dollar tumbled Thursday to its lowest level against the yen in nearly 18 months as Japanese officials signaled they wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an attempt to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The greenback traded as low as Yen107.69, its lowest level since Oct. 29, 2014, which was a few days before the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  shocked the market ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/japan-central-bank-shocks-market-with-fresh-easing-2014-10-31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/japan-\b  \highlight22central-bank\b0 \highlight22 -shocks-market-with-fresh-easing-2014-10-31}}}\uc2 ) with a massive expansion of its monthly asset purchases.\par \par \uc2 Though the buck pared its drop slightly to trade at Yen108.25 late Thursday in New York, compared with Yen109.79 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the year, the dollar has shed more than 10% of its value against the Japanese yen as concerns about global growth have ratcheted up demand for safe haven assets and expectations of a slower pace of interest rate increases at the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  sapped demand for the buck.\par \par \uc2 Market strategists struggled for a cohesive explanation for the yen's resilience so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Jane Foley, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 , noted that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained elevated even as risk assets have recovered--a sign that investors are holding on to worries that the extreme volatility from the beginning of the year could return.\par \par \uc2 "People are concerned that those factors haven't entirely gone away," Foley said.\par \par \uc2 Read:What the dollar, euro and yen have in store for the stock market ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/what-the-dollar-euro-and-yen-have-in-store-for-the-stock-market-2016-04-06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/what-the-dollar-euro-and-yen-have-in-store-for-the-stock-market-2016-04-06}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials, including Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 , have spoken out against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days, and many strategists believe the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't approve of such a move.\par \par \uc2 Abe said in an interview with The Wall Street Journal, when asked about recent strength in the yen, "we must definitely avoid competitive devaluation, and I think we should refrain from arbitrary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said Thursday the BOJ will "undertake additional monetary easing measures" either through enlarging its asset purchases or pushing its deposit rate further into negative territory, or both, to achieve its 2% inflation target if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Despite the drop in the yen, the \uc2 ICE\uc2  U.S. Dollar index, a gauge of the buck's value against a basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , remained buoyant, up 0.1% to 94.4740. as the euro and pound weakened.\par \par \uc2 The shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.1374 late Thursday in New York, compared with $1.1400 late Wednesday. Meanwhile, the British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.4062, compared with $1.4132 late Wednesday in New York.\par \par \uc2 Analysts blamed the Netherlands' rejection of an associational agreement with Ukraine for the weakness in the pound. The vote, a clear victory for euroskeptics, was seen as reigniting fears that voters in the U.K. will decide to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 07, 2016 15:59 ET (19:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160407ec470038n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
