\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Strength Reflects Loss of Faith in BoJ -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2016\par 19:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 13:59 ET - The yen's recent strength has been driven by a growing view the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  won't be able to accomplish its goals, says Nathan Thooft at John Hancock Asset Management. The dollar has retreated more than 10% against the yen so far this year and he says the move might not be done. Thooft has trimmed his exposure to Japanese stocks, on a hedged basis, to neutral. "The whole thesis on Japanese equities was that if they could win the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war and get their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak enough, it would support exports--which would therefore support earnings growth." (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 1717 GMT - \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says even though some market participants fear eurozone corporate bonds could be under selling pressure once \uc2 the ECB\uc2  starts buying them in June, it's likely to be "limited." In the past, investors flocked into covered- and sovereign-bond markets ahead of \uc2 ECB\uc2  purchases to later sell them, pushing yields back up once the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually moved into action. The investment bank says corporate bonds are bought by "dedicated specialist investors," which means purchases are likely to be "stickier than elsewhere." (jon.sindreu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:02 ET - A lawyer representing investors in Puerto Rico's senior sales-tax bonds says it's "understandable" the US commonwealth adopted a debt moratorium law Wednesday, given the slow pace of efforts to secure help from the US. House Republicans have proposed a bill that would allow the US commonwealth authority to restructure debt under the supervision of a federal control board. "With entrenched private institutions obstructing the legislative process in Washington, it is understandable that Puerto Rican leaders are taking steps to equip the island with the tools it needs," said Susheel Kirpalani, an attorney for Quinn Emmanuel. "COFINA Senior Bondholders hope our fellow creditors acknowledge this dire reality and finally stop holding legislation hostage." (aaron.kuriloff@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 12:55 ET - The bar is high for the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 --especially unilaterally--in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, so analysts are starting to wonder whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may announce fresh stimulus later this month in an effort to keep a lid on the yen. "The BoJ may well find itself between a rock and a hard place should JPY strength persist," says Viraj Patel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ING. "With \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely this side of Y105, the BoJ's biggest challenge will be to deliver a stimulus package that does more good than harm." He adds: "Getting it wrong could prove costly in terms of fuelling JPY upside." The dollar was recently down 1.5% at Y108.13. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 12:25 ET - Here's a catch from the soaring yen--it could dim Japanese investors' appetite to load up on Treasurys. A stronger dollar--or weaker yen--the past year and a half has been part of the reasons stoking demand for US debt because income from the US was inflated when converting back to yen. But this year the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been soaring and recent data showed investors there sold $14.2B in overseas notes and bonds the week ended April 1 after buying a net $10.4B the week before, says CRT Capital. Still, Japanese investors boosted demand for foreign bonds in February and March as a whole, so it may be premature to jump to conclusions. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 1624 GMT Russian equities and the ruble decline again as Brent crude futures drop back to $39 per barrel. The ruble-traded Micex index sheds 0.07% to 1858.85, its dollar-traded peer RTS declines 0.47% to 859.24. The ruble weakens, with USD/RUB up 0.8% to 68.13 rubles. The market mood is also soured by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecasts that the economy won't return to growth in coming months. \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  loses 0.21%, though \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  adds 0.47% and VTB is up 0.64%. Veles Capital brokerage says the Russian stock market is likely to continue falling on Friday, tracking its global peers.(andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:56 ET - No tools exist to accurately measure overall foreign investment in Canadian real estate, the country's federal housing agency says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canada Mortgage and Housing Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  made the comment in a report on condominium ownership that found foreign buyers in Toronto and Vancouver were more likely to own condos built after 2010 than condos built earlier. The study comes several weeks after Ottawa earmarked C$500,000 for Canada's statistics agency to study the issue more closely and confirms what many observers already knew: "At this time, no existing tool can provide a definitive measure of the level of foreign investment in Canada's housing markets." (kim.mackrael@wsj.com; @kimmackrael)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:54 ET - The risk-off trade that's sending investors into the yen is also pushing them out of the Australian dollar, which is down 1.4% against the greenback today. Part of that selloff can be chalked up to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which said Tuesday that a strengthening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be an impediment to the economy. "We heard more of a dovish tone from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," says David Song, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at DailyFX. But the outsize moves today are picking up as investors sell risk assets and buy safe ones. That's pushed the yen up 1.6% against the US dollar as the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise builds momentum. "Some of these moves may continue over the near-term," says Song. Elsewhere, fellow safe haven gold is up 1.5% while the S&P 500 drops 0.9% and high-grade copper futures are down 2.9%. (ben.eisen@wsj.com; @beneisen)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1510 GMT Alliander will be looking to finance its smart grid/smart meter programs with its debut Green bond, the Dutch utility's treasurer has confirmed. Mr. Ivo Kok says that a potion will also be earmarked for its energy-neutral Dijkgraaf 4 building in the Dutch town of Duiven. The transaction will mark the utility's debut in the Green Bond market. Alliander is understood to have enough liquidity to redeem the EUR400 million bond, which is due in two weeks' time, so no separate 'conventional bond' issue is on the cards. A roadshow is scheduled before the potential Green Bond issue, starting next Tuesday. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:09 ET - Valeant (VRX) bonds get a further lift as the drug maker has reached a deal with lenders which extends the deadline for filing its 2015 annual report past April 29 if needed. Not only does the deal diminish the threat of default, concessions to lenders also push the company in a more debtholder-friendly direction. VRX will be required to pay down loans with asset-sale proceeds and has a strong incentive to improve its balance sheet as doing so will reduce loan interest rates and give the company more freedom to pay dividends and make acquisitions. VRX's 6.125% bond due 2025 trade at 82.25c on the dollar, versus 81.25c yesterday and 77.5c a week ago, according to MarketAxess. Shares gain 5.7%, putting the week's bounce at 29%. (sam.goldfarb@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1459 GMT BNP Paribas Asset Management says it is now short GBP versus the USD. On a real effective exchange rate basis it argues that sterling is "neutral to expensive" versus the U.S. dollar. "Recently, there have been cracks in the U.K. growth outlook and the budget perspective," it says, while noting the U.K.'s current account and trade deficits. It adds the U.K. has recently seen lower inflows of foreign direct investment while the pound "also faces political risks." GBP/USD trades down 0.2% at $1.4106. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1454 GMT USD/JPY extends losses, dipping below the 108 mark to a fresh 17-month low around 107.86, with analysts saying traders are becoming bolder in the view that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at current levels. Some analysts see the yen as undervalued, while they also cite repatriation flows as Japanese investors take profit on substantial holdings in foreign assets. "The yen is undervalued, and at the same time Japan has a huge current account surplus," says Dankse Bank analyst Mikael Olai Milhoj. Additionally, analysts say investors see selling USD/JPY as the obvious way to short the USD in the wake of dovish \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  minutes.(jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 07, 2016 13:59 ET (17:59 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160407ec47002tk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
