\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Fed's policy caution sends dollar to 17-month low against yen\b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2016\par 13:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Dollar falls to around 108 yen, lowest since October 2014\par \par \uc2 * Fed minutes show members' concern about risks to growth\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF official says ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Updates prices, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 7 (Reuters) - The yen powered to a 17-month high against the dollar on Thursday, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure after minutes of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's meeting last month underscored its caution about future interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 The yen's surge, up around 9.5 percent against the dollar this year despite the imposition of negative rates, led to more warnings of action from the Japanese, who are concerned about a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dampening exports.\par \par \uc2 A senior \uc2 Japanese finance ministry\uc2  official said steps would be taken in the market as needed, and Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda also repeated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would ease policy further if needed, but there are doubts over how effective that would be.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 1.4 percent to 108.02 yen, its weakest against its Japanese counterpart since October 2014. The euro slid to 123.32 yen, its lowest in a month, with subdued stock markets also underpinning the safe-haven yen.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a broad-based soft dollar environment, and given the yen is cheap in relation to its long-term fundamentals, it is not surprising it is outperforming," said ING \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Petr Krpata.\par \par \uc2 "The rise is leading to speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese," Krpata added. "But we think the bar for that is pretty high and we are not seeing any major risk-off event."\par \par \uc2 The market is sceptical about the chances of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a \uc2 G7\uc2  summit that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hosting in May, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 YEN FOCUS\par \par \uc2 "(Prime Minister Shinzo) Abe does not want to get into trouble at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit for the BOJ focussing too much on the yen," said Commerzbank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Anthe Praefcke.\par \par \uc2 "Once the visitors have left, he or Kuroda can refer to 'disorderly movements' and 'excessive volatility' on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to their hearts content - the two tolerated exemptions for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - so as to be able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen," Praefcke said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which tracks it against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell to 94.015, its lowest since October 2015. It recovered to 94.414, still flat on the day. Traders will watch for comments from Fed chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , who takes part in a panel discussion later in the day.\par \par \uc2 Minutes from the Fed's March 15-16 policy meeting suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to raise interest rates before June, due to widespread concern among policymakers over their limited ability to counter the blow of a global slowdown.\par \par \uc2 The minutes showed debate over whether they might increase rates in April, with "a number" of them arguing that headwinds to growth would probably persist, and many urging caution about raising rates.\par \par \uc2 The euro was down 0.2 percent at $1.13805, not far from a 5-1/2 month high of $1.1438 touched last week. Minutes of the last \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting will be released on Thursday, with traders also looking to a speech later in the day by its president, \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 . (Additional reporting by Masayuki Kitano; Editing by John Stonestreet and David Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-7T12:09:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160407ec470106t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
