\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Touches Fresh 17-month Low Vs. Yen After Fed Minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2016\par 21:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Joseph Adinolfi, \uc2 MarketWatch\uc2  , Hiroyuki Kachi\par \par \uc2 Fed minutes show a 'healthy debate' about when to raise interest rates continues\par \par \uc2 The dollar briefly touched another 17-month low against. the yen Wednesday after the release of minutes from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's March meeting showed signs of uncertainty about when to raise interest rates next.\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded as low as $1.0934 after the minutes, but soon pared its drop to Yen109.59 in recent trade. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at Yen109.31 late Tuesday in New York.\par \par \uc2 But the buck's reaction was somewhat volatile, though. There appeared to be some disagreement among members of the Fed's policy setting committee as to the timing of the next hike, which lent the minutes a slightly hawkish flavor, said Boris Schlossberg, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BK Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 While sentiment was overwhelmingly tilted toward the cautious approach described by Fed Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  in a talk at the Economic Club of New York last week, the minutes showed that a healthy debate continues, including questions about whether inflation would hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target level ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-fed-is-split-on-this-crucial-economic-question-march-minutes-show-2016-04-06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-fed-is-split-on-this-crucial-economic-question-march-minutes-show-2016-04-06}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Some Fed officials in recent weeks have publicly advocated for a hike at the Fed's April meeting or soon thereafter. On Wednesday, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  published an interview with Kansas City Fed President \uc2 Esther George\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nytimes.com/2016/04/07/upshot/q-and-a-with-esther-george-a-fed-dissident-but-a-modest-one.html?_r=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.nytimes.com/2016/04/07/upshot/q-and-a-with-esther-george-a-fed-dissident-but-a-modest-one.html?_r=0}}}\uc2 ), where she laid out an argument for raising rates sooner rather than later.\par \par \uc2 Read: The probability of an April rate hike just doubled ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-probability-of-an-april-rate-hike-just-doubled-2016-03-23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-probability-of-an-april-rate-hike-just-doubled-2016-03-23}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Also read: April could be a crucial month for the yen and Japanese stocks ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/april-could-be-a-crucial-month-for-the-yen-and-japanese-stocks-2016-04-05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/april-could-be-a-crucial-month-for-the-yen-and-japanese-stocks-2016-04-05}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The fact that "there were several members who wanted a rate hike now suggests that there's clearly some discord on the committee," Schlossberg said.\par \par \uc2 Even before the minutes, the dollar experienced quite a bit of volatility against the yen on Wednesday. Early in the session, the greenback logged a sharp rise against its Japanese rival that caught the attention of many traders and strategists.\par \par \uc2 Read:Wall Street is wagering that the 'great dollar correction' is just beginning ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/wall-street-is-wagering-that-the-great-dollar-correction-is-just-beginning-2016-04-05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/wall-street-is-wagering-that-the-great-dollar-correction-is-just-beginning-2016-04-05}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The yen's persistent strength against the dollar so far this year has fueled speculation among traders and analysts that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from further strengthening. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was up nearly 9% against its U.S. rival since the beginning of the year in recent trade. A stronger yen can be a headwind to the BOJ' s efforts to implement easing measures to boost its flagging economy, making exports more expensive.\par \par \uc2 Recent comments from Japanese lawmakers and BOJ officials would suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 Early Wednesday, Japanese lawmaker Keiichiro Tachibana, a member of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, said the economy could tolerate the yen further appreciating against the buck to around Yen100. Those comments follow those from BOJ Governor Haruhiko Kuroda, who said the BOJ isn't targeting the exchange-rate.\par \par \uc2 A team of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at Scotiabank noted that the BOJ hasn't officially \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since 2011.\par \par \uc2 "What we're hearing out of Japan right now is that they're ready to step back in the markets and allow the yen to strengthen," said Doug Borthwick, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 Chapdelaine & Co\uc2 . "I would expect to hear some jawboning but I can't imagine we're going to see any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Central bankers' comments can be effective in influencing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 Borthwick attributed Wednesday's move to investor skittishness, saying moves higher in the dollar could easily snowball.\par \par \uc2 Central banks typically don't advertise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and traders on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales desks are often reluctant to discuss it.\par \par \uc2 The dollar performed slightly better against the euro and the pound after the minutes. The shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.1406 in recent trade, compared with $1.1384 late Tuesday in New York. The British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.4163, compared with $1.4163 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ICE\uc2  U.S. Dollar index, a measure of the buck's strength against a basket of six rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was up by less than 0.1% at 94.6677.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 06, 2016 15:23 ET (19:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160406ec460039s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
