\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar bounces back after hitting lows on Fed dovishness\b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 16:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Dollar rebounds from multi-month lows against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Focus on how Japanese authorities respond to firmer yen\par \par \uc2 * Dollar down vs emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Updates to U.S. trading, changes byline, dateline, previous London)\par \par \uc2 By Dion Rabouin\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 18 (Reuters) - The dollar recovered from a five-month low on Friday, rising against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as traders covered short positions after two straight days of selling in the wake of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's cautious view on global market developments.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the greenback against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was up 0.15 percent in tight trading but analysts said doubt remained that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would regain its footing in the near term.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was flat against the yen after moving up from a 17-month low on Thursday, with traders worried that a sharp rise in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would elicit some kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at 111.45 yen, off a low of 110.67 plumbed on Thursday that was its weakest since October 2014. The euro retreated from a five-week high of $1.1342 , falling 0.2 percent to $1.1294.\par \par \uc2 "It's been a dizzying selloff for the dollar, so it's natural that you're going to get some kind of bounce," said \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics partner David Gilmore in Essex, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's rebound from the previous days' lows was limited in part by the continued strength of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The potential of further dollar weakness, along with more accommodative moves from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , which both hold negative interest rates, has been a boon for emerging markets, said Win Thin, global head of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has fallen sharply since the Fed lowered its expectations for interest rate increases this year at the midweek Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging markets have economies tied to exporting and a weaker dollar is beneficial because it lowers the price of commodities like oil, coffee and metals, increasing those countries' profits. Many emerging market countries also hold debt in dollars, which is reduced when the dollar's value is lower.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against the oil-linked Mexican peso and Russian rouble, slipping 0.3 percent and 0.8 percent respectively. The dollar was also lower against the South African rand, which added 0.75 percent against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at or near lows for the year against all three \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I thought we'd see a little bit more profit-taking, but it seems like people are still feeling good enough about this EM bounce to stay long through the weekend and go into next week," Thin said. (Reporting by Dion Rabouin; Editing by Andrea Ricci) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-3-18T16:53:30.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160318ec3i01hmm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
