\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Japan Plan Runs Into a Wall\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi   \par \uc2 856 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 12:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's achievements from three years of monetary easing are unwinding, highlighting the limits central bankers face in trying to jolt an economy out of the doldrums.\par \par \uc2 Exhibit A is the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a key cog in the BOJ's plans. The yen rose Thursday to its strongest level since the day BOJ Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda unleashed a second monetary "bazooka" in October 2014. Its gains are undoing what that additional monetary easing was meant to accomplish.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese economy, meanwhile, is in trouble. Corporate profits, no longer inflated by a weak yen, are faltering. Tokyo's benchmark stock index remains 20% below its June 2015 peak. Inflation including energy is stuck near zero, and some measures of inflation expectations are at their lowest since Mr. Kuroda took over in early 2013.\par \par \uc2 It all adds up to growing skepticism at home and overseas about the BOJ's radical efforts to "reflate" Japan's economy with monetary policy. And it bodes ill for others, such as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that are struggling with the sort of stagnation that has afflicted Japan for two decades.\par \par \uc2 In Tokyo Wednesday, Nobel Prize-winning economist Joseph Stiglitz delivered a tough message to Japanese policy makers about their continuing efforts to reverse the tide with monetary easing-- most recently negative interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy has largely run its course," Mr. Stiglitz said at the meeting, attended by Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  and Mr. Kuroda. Negative rates are unlikely to stimulate growth, he said, while quantitative easing--the BOJ's mammoth asset-buying program--has increased inequality and failed to spur any significant increase in investment.\par \par \uc2 The asset buying, a pillar of the "Abenomics" growth program, dramatically weakened the yen between 2013 and the summer of 2015. That helped send corporate profits to all-time highs and stock prices sharply higher, while briefly stoking inflation.\par \par \uc2 But that initial success, which never translated into robust economic growth, was partly due to favorable global conditions. The U.S. economy was on a healthier growth track and many thought the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  would raise rates more aggressively--a prospect that made the dollar more attractive to investors versus the lower-yielding yen.\par \par \uc2 Much has changed. At a policy meeting Wednesday, the Fed dialed back the expected pace of its rate increases as a more vulnerable U.S. economy faces weakening global growth. "Caution is appropriate," Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Global market turmoil in January sent the yen sharply higher, as investors sold riskier assets. With Japan's economy having shrunk the previous quarter, Mr. Kuroda soon turned to negative rates, announcing a minus 0.1% rate on some bank reserves. To the puzzlement of BOJ economists, this failed to stem the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains significantly weaker than before Mr. Kuroda introduced his easing program in April 2013. But even at its current level, yen strength will further cut into Japanese corporate profits, which fell nearly 10% during the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 This is already disrupting Mr. Kuroda's critical "virtuous cycle," in which a weaker yen boosts profits, leading to higher wages and self-sustaining consumption and growth. In a blow to Messrs. Kuroda and Abe, \uc2 Toyota Motor Corp\uc2 . and many other big manufacturers on Wednesday announced smaller base-pay raises for the financial year starting in April.\par \par \uc2 The pay increases were nowhere near the level needed to achieve the BOJ's target of 2% inflation, a person close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acknowledged. There is now a growing sense at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the late-2017 target date for reaching 2% inflation--moved back three times already--isn't achievable.\par \par \uc2 Dealing with an economy that may be on the brink of a third technical recession in four years and BOJ goals that remain elusive, Japanese policy makers are at least tacitly acknowledging that monetary policy alone won't be enough. Advisers to Mr. Abe have lately focused on the need for fiscal stimulus, and postponing a planned sales-tax increase.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kuroda toughened his rhetoric this week as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose. He told lawmakers Wednesday that he could bring the deposit rate to as low as minus 0.5%--a shift from his previous approach of not emphasizing possible further cuts so as to avoid unnerving Japanese politicians and households. Minutes of the BOJ's meeting in late January also showed that board members debated expanding its asset buying.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policy makers may have to live with a stronger yen. Many predict further gains ahead, and European and U.S. officials have warned \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market or try to "talk it down."\par \par \uc2 "The hurdle to conduct yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is even higher than thought before," said Junya Tanase, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Securities.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, recently at Yen111.43, could fall to Yen103 by the end of the year, he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 18, 2016 07:13 ET (11:13 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160318ec3i0019l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
