\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei Slips Again As BoJ Frets Over Soaring Yen -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shuli Ren   \par \uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 01:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Poor, poor Japan!\par \par \uc2 While the rest of the world is partying over the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's dovish tone on rate hikes, Japan is slipping away.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 falls for a 4th day, down 1.6% this morning in Tokyo, as the Japanese yen rose 0.36% to 111.03. Overnight, the yen fell to as low as 110.67 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is obviously worried about soaring yen. A stronger yen ties business executives' hands to raise wages and move investments back home.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal's Kosaku Narioka reported that BoJ was checking yen rates during the U.S. trading hours overnight - a prelude to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? He wrote:\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were checking rates for the yen against the dollar earlier, a person familiar with the matter said Thursday, an indication of growing concern among Japanese authorities over the yen's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities in the past have demonstrated their uneasiness over the yen's rapid appreciation by calling banks and asking at what prices the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be bought and sold.\par \par \uc2 Reuters later reported BoJ was just asking about the causes of the yen moves and not checking rates. In other words, no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is eminent:\par \par \uc2 "It's not a rate check," the source told Reuters, when asked about a report that the BOJ was asking participants specific details about their dollar/yen positions, a move often seen as a threat or precursor to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rather, he said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "asking, 'Why is it moving?'" the source said.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, the \uc2 iShares MSCI Japan ETF\uc2  (EWJ) gained 0.4% thanks to the stronger yen, the \uc2 iShares \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Hedged MSCI Japan ETF\uc2  (HEWJ) fell 0.7%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Asia Stocks to Watch blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 17, 2016 20:53 ET (00:53 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160318ec3i0003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
