\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Gives Up Gains; Pound Falls Below $1.40\b0\par\par\uc2 By Min Zeng   \par \uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2016\par 23:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen ended the session little changed Wednesday after rising earlier against the dollar and reaching its strongest level versus the euro in nearly three years.\par \par \uc2 The buying in the yen was the strongest during the morning session, when a decline in the prices of crude oil and U.S. stocks stoked demand for haven assets. The yen gradually gave up its strength in the afternoon as equity and oil prices recovered.\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was Yen112.145 in late afternoon trading, compared with Yen112.108 Tuesday, according to data provider CQG. The dollar sank to Yen111.400 earlier in the session and approached its lowest level of the year.\par \par \uc2 The euro was near flat at Yen123.445. It earlier fell below Yen123 and reached its lowest level since April 2013.\par \par \uc2 Shaun Osborne, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotiabank, said the dollar would fall below Yen110 if sentiment sours again on riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 The yen has climbed more than 6% against the dollar since the start of the year as worries over the global economic outlook has driven many investors to cut holdings of riskier assets and preserve capital. The dollar fell to Yen110.985 on Feb. 11, its lowest intraday level since October 2014.\par \par \uc2 A stronger yen hurts the competitiveness of Japanese exports and raises the risk that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 Still, \uc2 Eric Viloria\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Wells Fargo Securities\uc2 , said the probability of the BOJ taking action remains "low," because what matters is "the pace of the yen's strength, not the levels."\par \par \uc2 Also Wednesday, the British pound fell below $1.40 for the first time since 2009 as investors continued to fret over the uncertainty surrounding the U.K.'s future in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the pound was down 0.6% at $1.3930. The pound also fell to the lowest level since December 2014 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The pound has been down since the start of the week as investors are concerned about the potential economic fallout if the U.K. exits the union. The U.K. referendum is set in June, and analysts say the uncertainty would continue to weigh on the British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors are using the pound as a vehicle to hedge their investments in the U.K.--from stocks, bonds to real estate in case the U.K. decides to bolt from the \uc2 EU\uc2 , known as Brexit, traders said. Foreign investment provides an important source of funding for the U.K.'s trade shortfall, so any large cutback would hurt the U.K.'s growth outlook and make the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less appealing to buy.\par \par \uc2 The uncertainty may push the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  to be more cautious in raising interest rates, another factor that would make the pound less attractive, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Douglas Borthwick\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 Chapdelaine & Co\uc2 ., a division of Tullett Prebon, said the pound could tumble to $1.20 or lower if the U.K. votes to leave the \uc2 EU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Borthwick, however, said he views the selloff as a buying opportunity because he doesn't expect Brexit to happen.\par \par \uc2 Investors also shed exposure to the euro on concerns about potential ripples from the U.K.'s possible exit from the \uc2 EU\uc2 , given the close economic and trade links between the eurozone and the U.K.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro earlier fell to a three-week low of $1.0958. In late afternoon trading, the euro recouped some loss to trade at $1.1014, partly driven by its strength against the pound.\par \par \uc2 A weak growth outlook for Europe could also be weighing on the euro, traders said. A report Tuesday showing a decline in business confidence in Germany raised concerns over the momentum in the eurozone's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 This bolstered the possibility of fresh monetary stimulus from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  when policy makers meet in March, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Ultraloose monetary policy--which often is tantamount to printing more money--reduces the value of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Min Zeng at min.zeng@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 24, 2016 17:03 ET (22:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160224ec2o004g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
