\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Dollar Strengthens Against Most Main Rivals -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Min Zeng   \par \uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2016\par 23:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar rose to a one-week high against the euro and the Swiss franc while reaching a two-week high versus the British pound as investors bet that global interest-rate policy outlook would favor a stronger buck.\par \par \uc2 The yen was the exception among the world's most actively traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , strengthening against the dollar following a two-day decline. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefited from haven demand as crude-oil prices fell.\par \par \uc2 The dollar is regaining some poise after taking a beating in the past few weeks. The swing comes as debate is heating up over how much room the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to strengthen after its sharp price gains since the summer of 2014.\par \par \uc2 The main boost for the dollar has been divergent paths of monetary policy. The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has been the only major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise short-term interest rates, which has attracted buyers on the prospect of higher returns.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has suffered a setback this month as many investors wonder whether the Fed may need to hold off raising rates this year out of concern that the U.S. economy could lose momentum amid market turmoil and weaker growth overseas.\par \par \uc2 Buyers embraced the dollar again after some recent data, including Friday's better-than-expected retail sales, eased anxiety. Fed Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  and other officials have continued to signal that their rate-increase campaign remains on track, albeit at a cautious pace.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials in the eurozone and Japan have signaled that more monetary stimulus may be in the pipeline. European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  reiterated Monday the commitment to act if needed. Many investors expect \uc2 the ECB\uc2  to take further action at its March policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 Investors say it is premature to declare the dollar's rally has run its course given the interest-rate policy backdrop. Money managers say they have become more selective this year in their bullish bets on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar's strength is likely to continue but at a measured pace," said Peter Gorra, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in New York at \uc2 BNP Paribas SA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading Tuesday, one euro bought $1.1143, compared with $1.1155 on Monday. Against the greenback, the British pound fell by 1%, the New Zealand dollar lost 1.2% and the Swiss franc was down 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ICE\uc2  dollar index, which values the dollar's strength against a number of its main peers, rose by 1% to 96.875 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The index had reached 100.51 in early December, the highest since 2003.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Gorra said the index could retest 100 but he doesn't expect much further gain above that mark.\par \par \uc2 The dollar could suffer more selling should the risk of a U.S. recession increases, as it would encourage investors to slash bullish wagers on the greenback, say traders.\par \par \uc2 Hedge funds and money managers accumulated $14.5 billion in bets that the dollar will rise for the week that ended Feb 9, according to data from Scotiabank. That is the lowest level since mid-October.\par \par \uc2 Fed funds futures, used by investors and traders to place bets on \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, showed Tuesday that they see a 28% likelihood of a rate increase from the Fed at its Dec 2016 policy meeting, according to data from \uc2 CME Group\uc2 . The probability was below 10% a week ago. But it had been more than 50% in late 2015.\par \par \uc2 The minutes of the Fed's January policy meeting is due Wednesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Robert Tipp\uc2 , chief investment strategist at \uc2 Prudential Financial Inc\uc2 .'s fixed- income division, which manages more than $500 billion, said he expects commodities-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Canadian dollar, the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar, to weaken more against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The theme of lower commodities is "still in place," which likely exerts downward pressure on commodities-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Mr. Tipp.\par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in particular has managed to break the dollar's bullish cycle.\par \par \uc2 The yen has been a big winner this year as global market turmoil boosted demand for haven assets. The yen last week rose to its strongest level against the dollar since October 2014, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touching 110.985 yen. For the year through Monday, the yen has rallied by 4.7% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In late Tuesday, one dollar bought Yen113.885, down from Yen114.600 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say further gains in the yen could raise the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A stronger yen makes Japanese exports less competitive, especially with global demand weak.\par \par \uc2 Write to Min Zeng at min.zeng@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 16-02-16 2226GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160216ec2g000hb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal6