\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2016\par 13:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 U.K. Inflation Gathered Steam in January\par \par \uc2 U. K. annual inflation rose in January to its highest rate in a year, suggesting price growth is set to slowly edge up throughout 2016 as the effect of past drops in commodity prices gradually wears off.\par \par \uc2 New Credit From Chinese Banks Hits Fresh High\par \par \uc2 New credit extended by Chinese banks hit a new high in January, as lenders front-loaded lending while companies cut foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt amid the weakening yuan.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Korea Leaves Policy Rate Unchanged\par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its policy rate unchanged, as expected, despite growing pressure to ease policy and help the economy.\par \par \uc2 German Finance Minister Says Market Volatility Is Affecting Economic Conditions\par \par \uc2 German Finance Minister \uc2 Wolfgang Sch\u228\'00\'E4uble\uc2  said that recent volatility in financial markets is affecting global economic conditions and financial officials from the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  nations will discuss how to deal with the current uncertainties.\par \par \uc2 China Premier Vows to Guard Against Financial Risks\par \par \uc2 China's Premier \uc2 Li Keqiang\uc2  pledged to step up efforts to stay vigilant against risks in the financial market, while reiterating that the country's economic fundamentals remain solid due to steady employment.\par \par \uc2 Japan Finance Minister: No New Stimulus Measures Planned\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso said he isn't considering any additional fiscal stimulus measures, playing down economic weakness over the winter months as a phenomenon caused by unusually warm weather.\par \par \uc2 Abe's Adviser Says Finance Ministry Should \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market\par \par \uc2 An adviser to Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb volatility in the yen, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rebound since last week is unusually sharp.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 16, 2016 07:51 ET (12:51 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160216ec2g001hg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
