\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Remains Steady Against Yen as Stocks in Asia Gain -3-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Hiroyuki Kachi   \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2016\par 07:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar remained steady against the yen in Asia trade Tuesday, with the strength in Asian stocks clearing up market sentiment to invite selling of haven assets.\par \par \uc2 At about 0450 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at Y114.68 after reaching as high as Y114.87 earlier in the Asia session. They are higher than Y114.58 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 With investors still feeling the heat from yesterday's Tokyo stocks rally, higher commodities prices and robust gains in Asian shares helped brighten the mood, prompting investors to sell the perceived safety of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Tokyo, the Nikkei Stock Average added 142.58 points, or 0.9%, to 16,165.16 midday after soaring 7.2% Monday. The Shanghai Composite Index was recently 2.8% higher at 2823.86.\par \par \uc2 "We are seeing unwinding of risk-off [yen buying] positions at a gradual pace, although it doesn't look dramatic," said Yuzo Sakai, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  business promotion at Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  & Ueda Harlow.\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Sakai said especially after the dollar's steep fall to below Y111 amid recent high volatility, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains vulnerable to selling on recovery if it comes closer to Y115, adding that the dollar will likely trade in a Y111-Y116 range for some time.\par \par \uc2 The yen has strengthened against the dollar, which briefly lost up to 9% against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in less than two weeks even with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's decision in late January to impose negative interest rates for the first time.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the dollar was almost flat against the euro, which was at $1.1156 compared with $1.1152 late Monday, after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't hesitate to boost its stimulus in March. Against the yen, the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at Y127.95 from Y127.89.\par \par \uc2 After recent yen volatility, investors showed muted reaction to comments from an adviser to Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 , who said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "The yen's recent appreciation is abnormal from statistical perspectives" and appears driven by hedge funds, said Koichi Hamada, one of Mr. Abe's close economic advisers and a Yale University professor emeritus, in a recent interview.\par \par \uc2 Effective Tuesday, the BOJ imposed a minus 0.1% interest rate on a portion of commercial banks' yen deposits at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But dealers and analysts said the action, which briefly sent the overnight call rate to 0% earlier in the day, had no impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index, a measure of the dollar against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was unchanged at 89.40.\par \par \uc2 Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rates At 23:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par USD/JPY Japan           114.69-70      114.60-61  +0.08   114.87   114.29  -4.66 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.1156-59      1.1153-56  +0.03   1.1185   1.1148  +2.73 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.4437-39      1.4435-37  +0.01   1.4457   1.4427  -2.02 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9877-81      0.9868-72  +0.09   0.9893   0.9855  -1.41 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.3752-57      1.3831-36  -0.57   1.3844   1.3750  -0.61 \par AUD/USD Australia       0.7151-55      0.7137-41  +0.20   0.7179   0.7131  -1.84 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.6591-97      0.6645-51  -0.81   0.6677   0.6590  -3.50 \par Euro Rates \par EUR/JPY Japan           127.93-97      127.82-86  +0.09   128.20   127.74  -2.17 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Tullett Prebon\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Hiroyuki Kachi at Hiroyuki.Kachi@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 16-02-16 0602GMT\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160216ec2g0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
