\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen on track for strongest week since late 2008\b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2016\par 13:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 Barclays\uc2  note on dollar/yen)\par \par \uc2 * Yen rise leads to speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yen volatility soars to highest since June 2013\par \par \uc2 * Euro off recent highs, trades below $1.13\par \par \uc2 By Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The yen was on track on Friday for its biggest weekly gain against the dollar since late 2008 as worries about global growth supported inflows to safe-haven assets, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent surge stalled in London trade.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials stepped up their attempts to talk the yen down, with Finance Minister Taro Aso hoping that the G20 finance leaders gathering in Shanghai this month will consider a global policy response to the recent market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Major central banks including the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  have all adopted negative rates to boost inflation. But these are weighing on banks' earnings and dragging down stocks globally, threatening business confidence and growth prospects.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was up 0.15 percent at 112.55 yen, having fallen to 110.985 yen on Thursday, its lowest level since October 2014. It was on track to shed 3.7 percent for the week, its worst since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had jumped to 113 yen in thin trading in Europe on Thursday, leading to speculation that Japanese authorities were checking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, a step that often precedes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A government official declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "The introduction of negative interest rates has certainly not weakened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Commerzbank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, Lutz Karpowitz, said. "Of course, that is not at all what the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  had hoped to achieve. The Japanese officials really need a weak yen unless they want their own inflation projections to become a laughing stock."\par \par \uc2 The yen's ascent followed the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's move to adopt negative interest rates on Jan. 29, under which banks have to pay interest on certain deposits held at the BOJ. The dollar hit a high of 121.70 yen, before sliding stocks, slowing Chinese growth and falling crude oil prices sent investors into perceived safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some traders said the dollar could to drop to 110 yen, a level not seen since late 2014, if risk appetite falls further. \uc2 Barclays\uc2  cut its dollar/yen forecasts, saying the greenback will fall to 95 yen by the end of the year - more than 20 percent lower than the 120 yen previously forecast.\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/yen implied volatility, an indicator of how much \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is expected in the weeks ahead, surged to 15.9 percent on Friday, its highest since June 2013, up more than seven points from levels seen this month.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.4 percent to $1.1280, not far Thursday's high of $1.1377, its highest since October 2015. (Editing by Louise Ireland) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-2-12T13:28:44.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160212ec2c00ezi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
