\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: Energy and Banks Lift Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 1,556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2016\par 12:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Markets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A rally in energy and banking shares lifted European markets Friday, even as Japan's main index fell to its lowest level in more than a year as it caught up with a sharp selloff in the previous session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 was up 1.8% in early trade.\par \par \uc2 Boosting sentiment, oil prices rallied, rebounding from a 13-year low the previous day, on speculation of production cuts among some of the world's biggest suppliers.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude, the global oil benchmark, rose 4.6% to $31.43 a barrel on London's \uc2 ICE\uc2  Futures exchange. On the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 , West Texas Intermediate futures were trading up 4.3% at $27.33 a barrel. WTI fell to $26.21 a barrel on Thursday, the lowest settlement since May 6, 2003.\par \par \uc2 Prices rose after the United Arab Emirates energy minister said late Thursday that members of the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  were ready to cooperate on possible production cuts. Venezuela, meanwhile, proposed that \uc2 OPEC\uc2  and non-OPEC producers should at least freeze output at the current level.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, banks stocks staged a relief rally to trade up 2.9%,\par \par \uc2 Shares in Germany's \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  soared 13.6% Friday after the bank said it would pay its first dividend for five years.\par \par \uc2 Still, the banks remain down 26% this year. European banks fell sharply Thursday on concerns over slowing global growth and the impact of negative interest rates on bank earnings.\par \par \uc2 Mining shares also surged. Gold fell 0.7% to $1238.80 an ounce, after gold gained 4.5% Thursday to its highest level in a year. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par American Markets Outlook: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wall Street was poised to bounce back from multiyear closing lows, as investors get the chance to go bargain hunting for shares beaten down in the market carnage.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also helping to calm nerves is a rally in oil prices, prompted by more hints that \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is ready to consider a cut in oil production.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures for the Dow Jones Industrial Average jumped 105 points, or 0.7%, to 15,715, while those for the S&P 500 index gained 12.50 points, or 0.7%, to 1,837. Futures for the Nasdaq 100 index rose 28.75, or 0.7%, to 3,990.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's data releases may give fresh insight into the impact of this year's market turmoil on the U.S. economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 First up are retail sales for January, due at 1330 GMT. They are forecast to show no growth last month, compared with a drop of 0.1% in December. At the same time, the import-price index for January is due.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1500 GMT come reports on consumer sentiment for February and business inventories in December. As for Federal Reserve speakers, New York Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  will give a speech on household borrowing and indebtedness at 1500 GMT. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news, RBC analysts had recommended long USD/JPY positions if yen extends recent steep gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the selloff extends through 110 toward 105, risk/reward favors being long spot, however heavy the momentum appears." USD/JPY began the week around the 117 level and dropped sharply after that, hitting around 111.0 in Asian trade Thursday and raising concerns about possible \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem JPY gains. RBC's model already puts the probability of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 15%. "If USD/JPY extends the selloff at a big figure a day for another week, this rises to 50%." RBC says \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may stabilise risk appetite, but notes USD/JPY is "undervalued".\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the euro was down 0.3% against the dollar at $1.1285, even after data showed Germany's economy remained on a steady yet modest growth path at the end of last year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par Top Stories: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone Economy Grows Steadily\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Robust domestic consumption kept Germany's economy on a steady yet modest growth path at the end of last year, despite weak exports and growing headwinds from the global economy, official data showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank Returns to Profit as Revenue Rises\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would pay its first dividend in five years and expects net profit to grow slightly this after swinging back into the black in the fourth quarter, helped by higher revenue and falling bad-loan provisions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rolls-Royce Cuts Dividend as Profit Falls\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rolls-Royce\f28 \uc2 \f2  has slashed its full-year dividend 39%, the first cut in its shareholder payment since 1992, though investors embraced the lack of further bad news prompting shares to rise more than 12%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian Banks Close In on Merger\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's Banco Popolare is closing in on a merger deal \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banca Popolare di Milano\f28 \uc2 \f2  that would create Italy's third largest banking group by assets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Analysis: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 'Flash Rally' in Eurodollar-Futures Contract Hints at Unease Over Fed\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A brief surge Thursday morning in the price of a popular derivative used to bet on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate moves is the latest sign of markets reacting in unexpected ways under stress.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Why Sweden's Negative Deposit Rate Isn't as Scary as It Looks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite appearances, the significance of a negative deposit rate is much bigger for \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  than it is for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Lender Worry: Oil Firms Max Out Credit Lines\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Struggling oil and gas companies are maxing out revolving credit lines typically used to cover short-term funding gaps, raising fresh concerns about banks' exposure to the decline in energy prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More Cuts Loom as Oil Nears $25\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As crude prices slide toward $25 a barrel, many oil companies have little choice but to start making the steep cost cuts they have avoided up until now, jettisoning every well that can't break even or isn't needed to keep the lights on.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Big Beneficiary of Negative Rates: Gold\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are piling into gold, seeking shelter amid concerns that a turn toward negative interest rates in some countries is threatening to destabilize the global financial system. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Still To Come \par Friday, February 12, 2016 \par GMT                    Exp   Prev \par 1330 US  Jan Import & Export \par              Price Indexes \par              Import   -1.5% -1.2% \par              Non-Petroleum  -0.4% \par              Petroleum     -10.0% \par 1330 US  Jan Advance Monthly \par              Sales for Retail